1
00:00:10,301 --> 00:00:13,138
THE LOVE LAB

2
00:00:13,221 --> 00:00:17,058
<i>Now, the third king's privilege</i>
<i>will be announced.</i>

3
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:17,976
Right away?

4
00:00:18,059 --> 00:00:19,728
<i>You cannot check</i>

5
00:00:19,811 --> 00:00:22,939
<i>your own Heart Boxes today.</i>

6
00:00:24,524 --> 00:00:25,817
<i>Only the king</i>

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,320
<i>can open everyone's Heart Box.</i>

8
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:35,785
<i>Only the king can see</i>
<i>the result of everyone's Heart Chip vote.</i>

9
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,203
-Even the notes?
-I want to do it.

10
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:38,747
I want to be king.

11
00:00:41,249 --> 00:00:43,001
<i>I think he voted for me,</i>

12
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:45,420
<i>and of course, Ga-yeon</i>

13
00:00:45,503 --> 00:00:49,591
since he voted for both of us
yesterday as well.

14
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:54,679
<i>I did think that Jung-min</i>
<i>and Kyung-ho probably voted for me,</i>

15
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:57,432
so I wasn't curious
about the number of hearts.

16
00:00:57,515 --> 00:00:59,434
I just wanted to see the notes.

17
00:00:59,517 --> 00:01:02,812
The first thing I wondered was
if they'll be delivered at some point.

18
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:06,107
And I also wondered
what I'd do if it didn't get delivered.

19
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:08,943
The message was something
that I really wanted to say.

20
00:01:09,444 --> 00:01:11,446
I wondered if Ga-yeon voted for me or not,

21
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,823
how much she put in,
and what she wrote on the note.

22
00:01:13,907 --> 00:01:15,241
I'm most curious about those.

23
00:01:15,825 --> 00:01:18,411
<i>If you are curious about your Heart Box,</i>

24
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:21,956
<i>you must win the favor of the king</i>
<i>to get the information.</i>

25
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:25,335
<i>Second,</i>

26
00:01:25,418 --> 00:01:28,546
<i>the king will find out</i>

27
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:31,049
<i>everyone's Heart Chip colors.</i>

28
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:31,966
Really?

29
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:33,676
-Nice.
-Must be nice.

30
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:34,594
Wow. Nice.

31
00:01:34,677 --> 00:01:36,513
The king gets to know everything, then.

32
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:39,766
<i>I was a bit taken aback when I heard that.</i>

33
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:44,354
<i>What am I supposed to do</i>
<i>after I look at all of that by myself?</i>

34
00:01:44,437 --> 00:01:46,773
<i>My head hurt a lot.</i>

35
00:01:46,856 --> 00:01:50,110
I thought I'd get the power
to choose the dates.

36
00:01:50,193 --> 00:01:54,322
To be honest, that's why
Ye-rim made me king.

37
00:01:55,657 --> 00:01:58,493
But because I didn't have
that important power,

38
00:01:58,576 --> 00:02:00,036
<i>I was startled.</i>

39
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:03,331
<i>Third, the king may choose</i>

40
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:08,169
<i>a man and woman</i>
<i>to spend the night in the tent.</i>

41
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:09,838
No way.

42
00:02:09,921 --> 00:02:11,256
-No way.
-No way.

43
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:12,549
Kyung-ho and Ye-rim?

44
00:02:12,632 --> 00:02:13,591
Seriously, no.

45
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:15,135
-Kyung-ho and Ye-rim…
-You go out.

46
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:19,139
Let me say this nicely,
you and Chae-rin should go out, okay?

47
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:21,850
I mean it.

48
00:02:22,350 --> 00:02:27,981
<i>…choose a man and woman</i>
<i>to spend the night in the tent.</i>

49
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:36,114
<i>Today's king, Park Do-geon,</i>

50
00:02:36,197 --> 00:02:37,699
<i>shall go to the Heart Room</i>

51
00:02:37,782 --> 00:02:41,202
<i>to check everyone's Heart Chip</i>
<i>and Heart Box.</i>

52
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:43,913
Sounds fun.

53
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:45,456
Should we carry you there?

54
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,751
-Sounds fun.
-See you.

55
00:02:48,835 --> 00:02:49,669
Okay.

56
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:51,337
Remember well this time.

57
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:56,634
He forgets everything.
Even the colors of his own hearts.

58
00:02:57,260 --> 00:02:58,720
He forgets mine too.

59
00:02:58,803 --> 00:03:01,764
I really did forget.

60
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,099
What's the color of your hearts?

61
00:03:03,182 --> 00:03:04,183
Isn't it pink?

62
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,643
ACTING LIKE SHE DOESN'T KNOW

63
00:03:05,727 --> 00:03:09,606
I don't know. I don't remember
the colors I got on the first day.

64
00:03:09,689 --> 00:03:10,940
Can you remember them?

65
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:13,026
I should take a piece of paper.

66
00:03:13,109 --> 00:03:14,193
Take some paper.

67
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:16,446
-Take a piece of paper?
-He seriously should.

68
00:03:21,034 --> 00:03:24,495
EVERYONE'S HEART CHIP JAR
HAS THEIR NAME ON IT

69
00:03:25,747 --> 00:03:28,917
EACH BOX SHOWS THE CURRENT
HEART CHIP STATUS AND NAMES OF THE VOTERS

70
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,293
HA-YOON: 66
YE-RIM: 205, CHAE-RIN: 1, HYE-WON: 26

71
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:31,878
JUNG-MIN: 63
DO-GEON: 24

72
00:03:31,961 --> 00:03:35,673
HYE-WON, HA-YOON, YE-RIM, JUNG-MIN,
DO-GEON, GA-YEON, CHAE-RIN, KYUNG-HO

73
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:38,885
CHECKING THE RESULT
OF HIS OWN HEART CHIPS FIRST

74
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:39,802
PARK DO-GEON

75
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:42,680
YE-RIM: 205, CHAE-RIN: 1, HYE-WON: 26

76
00:03:45,016 --> 00:03:48,353
PARK DO-GEON, GONGGI
GOOD LUCK!

77
00:03:48,436 --> 00:03:51,397
TIME TO GO ON A DATE WITH ME

78
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:55,026
<i>I felt sure about Chae-rin</i>
<i>after seeing that.</i>

79
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,366
<i>I was most curious about</i>
<i>where Kyung-ho's feelings</i>

80
00:04:01,449 --> 00:04:03,201
<i>were leaning toward.</i>

81
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:04,994
I'M ROOTING FOR THE QUEEN

82
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:08,248
GA-YEON'S BOX
KYUNG-HO: 40, JUNG-MIN: 16

83
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:11,751
<i>Since Kyung-ho voted for Ga-yeon,</i>

84
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:16,881
<i>I figured he has feelings for her.</i>

85
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:20,260
<i>But when I read his note,</i>

86
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:22,595
<i>he told her to choose what she wants.</i>

87
00:04:22,679 --> 00:04:26,933
<i>I recall it being a long note</i>
<i>with that kind of message on it.</i>

88
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:27,976
<i>After seeing that,</i>

89
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:30,645
<i>I thought, "What does that mean?"</i>

90
00:04:30,728 --> 00:04:33,231
<i>Then, are these Heart Chips</i>

91
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:36,859
<i>his final message to her?</i>

92
00:04:37,652 --> 00:04:40,697
<i>I thought it was very vague.</i>

93
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:44,409
KING DO-GEON WRITES THEM DOWN
SO HE WON'T FORGET

94
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:46,119
MEANWHILE, IN THE LIVING ROOM

95
00:04:46,202 --> 00:04:47,996
Who voted for Do-geon?

96
00:04:49,247 --> 00:04:50,248
No one fell for that.

97
00:04:50,331 --> 00:04:52,250
-The women did.
-I didn't…

98
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,628
Someone made a deal with Do-geon

99
00:04:56,379 --> 00:04:59,299
and promised to give him
a bunch of hearts.

100
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:01,592
Like 100 hearts. All for Do-geon.

101
00:05:01,676 --> 00:05:04,554
-It could have been 200.
-Yeah, 200.

102
00:05:04,637 --> 00:05:07,098
"Let's get along."

103
00:05:07,682 --> 00:05:10,727
"You're the puppet king.
I'm the real king."

104
00:05:11,227 --> 00:05:13,146
It could have been something like that.

105
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:15,189
That's jumping to conclusions though.

106
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:21,195
<i>I was in a really foul mood</i>
<i>after he said that.</i>

107
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:23,573
I did go on a date with Do-geon

108
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:26,951
and I didn't think that
Kyung-ho wouldn't know

109
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:30,246
about my alliance or plot with Do-geon.

110
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:35,793
Did he have to say that
in front of everyone?

111
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:39,881
Is he saying that
because he didn't like what I did?

112
00:05:39,964 --> 00:05:41,716
He said "puppet king" sarcastically.

113
00:05:44,135 --> 00:05:45,887
Can the king not choose the dates then?

114
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:48,264
Today's camping is going to be important.

115
00:05:48,765 --> 00:05:51,267
He's going to see all the notes I wrote.

116
00:05:52,685 --> 00:05:53,519
That's annoying.

117
00:05:53,603 --> 00:05:55,146
What did you write?

118
00:05:55,229 --> 00:05:57,607
-How cheesy was it?
-Did you propose to her?

119
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:00,526
I think Do-geon's expression
is going to be hilarious.

120
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:06,532
DO-GPT OVERLOAD

121
00:06:07,658 --> 00:06:11,120
JUST THEN, A HEART BOX
CAUGHT DO-GEON'S EYE

122
00:06:11,204 --> 00:06:12,914
LEE YE-RIM

123
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:16,209
0 HEARTS

124
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:18,294
MOMENTS AGO

125
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:21,881
KYUNG-HO PUT HEART CHIPS
INTO GA-YEON'S BOX

126
00:06:27,386 --> 00:06:29,847
KYUNG-HO DID NOT PUT
ANY HEART CHIPS INTO YE-RIM'S BOX

127
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:35,186
<i>Honestly, I had no idea</i>
<i>what I could do for her.</i>

128
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:40,858
<i>Was telling her everything</i>
<i>the right thing to do or staying quiet?</i>

129
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:43,528
<i>I was feeling overwhelmed.</i>

130
00:06:45,488 --> 00:06:48,241
<i>If I told her the truth,</i>

131
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:50,910
<i>it may hurt her rather than help her.</i>

132
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:53,121
<i>So I was very cautious.</i>

133
00:06:57,542 --> 00:06:59,377
-The king has returned.
-Oh, no.

134
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,629
Gosh. I'm done being king.

135
00:07:01,712 --> 00:07:02,922
Come here.

136
00:07:03,005 --> 00:07:04,215
Please leave.

137
00:07:07,844 --> 00:07:10,179
-He wrote them down.
-He has a lot of paper.

138
00:07:11,764 --> 00:07:12,723
I see.

139
00:07:15,476 --> 00:07:16,519
-What?
-I see.

140
00:07:16,602 --> 00:07:18,062
What's up with him?

141
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:18,980
Oh, I see.

142
00:07:19,063 --> 00:07:20,940
-What is it that you see?
-What is it?

143
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:23,484
Are those the notes you wrote down?

144
00:07:23,568 --> 00:07:24,652
-The ones you recorded?
-Take them.

145
00:07:24,735 --> 00:07:26,654
-Let's knock him out.
-Take them from him.

146
00:07:26,737 --> 00:07:29,115
If you're curious about anything,

147
00:07:29,198 --> 00:07:30,491
win my favor.

148
00:07:31,993 --> 00:07:33,327
I can tell you if you want.

149
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:34,662
-Really,
-Yes.

150
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:36,581
sir?

151
00:07:38,207 --> 00:07:39,041
"Sir?"

152
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,793
I have to decide who sleeps outside.

153
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:42,295
That's right.

154
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:44,172
I really want to

155
00:07:44,255 --> 00:07:45,923
sleep inside.

156
00:07:46,007 --> 00:07:47,633
Your face is radiant today.

157
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:49,760
It has been radiant this whole time.

158
00:07:50,344 --> 00:07:52,805
Should the person who thinks they'll go
try to win him over?

159
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,557
If you have a bad feeling about it?

160
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,809
-I have a bad feeling about me.
-I do.

161
00:07:56,893 --> 00:07:58,102
I really do.

162
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:02,231
Close your eyes and I'll pick two people.

163
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,275
-Those two can go.
-Okay.

164
00:08:05,818 --> 00:08:07,445
Are you thinking straight, Do-geon?

165
00:08:07,528 --> 00:08:08,696
I'm counting on you.

166
00:08:08,779 --> 00:08:11,741
I can't wait to see
how Do-geon handles this.

167
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:14,076
-Don't pick Ye-rim!
-I think he'll pick Ye-rim.

168
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:14,994
I'm scared.

169
00:08:15,077 --> 00:08:16,454
Oh. Please don't?

170
00:08:16,537 --> 00:08:18,998
We have to be like,
"Please don't pick us."

171
00:08:19,582 --> 00:08:20,500
I'm scared.

172
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:25,338
I'm really scared.

173
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,091
Do-geon, please.

174
00:08:29,842 --> 00:08:33,262
HE CHOOSES YE-RIM TO SLEEP IN THE TENT

175
00:08:36,849 --> 00:08:38,100
HE CHOOSES KYUNG-HO TO SLEEP IN THE TENT

176
00:08:38,184 --> 00:08:39,268
Okay, I'm done choosing.

177
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:42,396
You see? You see?

178
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:45,066
How is she supposed to sleep?

179
00:08:45,149 --> 00:08:47,693
-It was as I expected.
-You know what? This is for the better.

180
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,237
They can make up overnight.

181
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:53,533
Ye-rim did want to
have a conversation with him.

182
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,868
-Instead of being frustrated…
-Yeah.

183
00:08:55,952 --> 00:08:58,371
-…it's better to talk one-on-one.
-Yeah.

184
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:00,039
Okay, I'm done choosing.

185
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:02,166
-Really?
-You chose?

186
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:03,960
-I'm really scared.
-Who was chosen?

187
00:09:04,043 --> 00:09:07,171
-I think it's these two.
-I think so too.

188
00:09:07,255 --> 00:09:08,631
-I know.
-That's my guess.

189
00:09:08,714 --> 00:09:10,550
-He didn't choose me though.
-Really?

190
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:11,759
He's acting.

191
00:09:11,842 --> 00:09:14,220
-He really didn't choose me.
-What?

192
00:09:14,303 --> 00:09:16,264
-Who was chosen?
-What?

193
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:17,181
It's you, isn't it?

194
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:20,184
It's me.

195
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:22,311
-Ye-rim and Kyung-ho?
-Is that right?

196
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:33,823
That feels weird.

197
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:34,865
Have fun.

198
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:35,866
Do we go now?

199
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:36,951
-What?
-No, later.

200
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:38,744
We can go later when we sleep.

201
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,872
<i>He must really not want to go.</i>

202
00:09:45,418 --> 00:09:47,336
He said it wasn't him.

203
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,463
He said he had a bad feeling
before it even started

204
00:09:49,547 --> 00:09:52,675
and he knew he would get chosen.

205
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:55,011
Did he have to be so obvious
that he didn't want to go?

206
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:56,470
The thing is,

207
00:09:56,554 --> 00:10:01,309
<i>everyone noticed that Kyung-ho and I</i>
<i>were initially interested in each other.</i>

208
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:10,484
And everyone knew that
the vibe changed after the first date.

209
00:10:10,568 --> 00:10:12,570
So did he have to go that far?

210
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:15,364
<i>I was very upset about that.</i>

211
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:18,159
THE 3RD KING STARTED RULING

212
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:20,620
-Let me get straight to the point.
-Okay.

213
00:10:20,703 --> 00:10:22,830
Kyung-ho voted for Ga-yeon.

214
00:10:22,913 --> 00:10:25,625
He gave her about 63 hearts.

215
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:26,709
Sixty…

216
00:10:26,792 --> 00:10:28,169
KYUNG-HO GAVE GA-YEON 40 HEARTS

217
00:10:28,252 --> 00:10:29,128
63 hearts?

218
00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:30,838
Kyung-ho gave her 40 hearts.

219
00:10:30,921 --> 00:10:32,298
He gave her 40 hearts.

220
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:33,758
And on the note,

221
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:34,675
well…

222
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:38,262
What did it say? Hang on.

223
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:42,725
Anyway, Ye-rim invested
her Heart Chips in me,

224
00:10:42,808 --> 00:10:44,852
I wanted to repay her kindness.

225
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:47,313
I had to repay Ye-rim's kindness.

226
00:10:47,396 --> 00:10:48,606
Hold on.

227
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:50,107
-Do-geon!
-He's so clumsy.

228
00:10:50,858 --> 00:10:54,111
He wrote something in the vein of
hoping she'd make her own choice.

229
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:55,863
"I'll make the choice for you."

230
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:57,865
THE HEART CHIP INFO GOES OFF TRACK

231
00:10:57,948 --> 00:11:02,036
If someone smart like Ha-yoon did it,
he would have done a good job.

232
00:11:02,119 --> 00:11:07,333
And when I looked carefully
at Kyung-ho's note…

233
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:09,543
So the reason why Kyung-ho

234
00:11:09,627 --> 00:11:11,212
voted for Ga-yeon was because

235
00:11:12,713 --> 00:11:14,173
he wanted to give her the note.

236
00:11:14,256 --> 00:11:15,549
He gave her 40 hearts to do that?

237
00:11:15,633 --> 00:11:16,759
I know, right?

238
00:11:16,842 --> 00:11:18,803
Maybe he wanted to make her king.

239
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:20,888
But Ga-yeon wanted to

240
00:11:21,430 --> 00:11:24,308
make Jung-min king.

241
00:11:24,392 --> 00:11:26,143
She gave him 163 hearts.

242
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,603
And she wrote,

243
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:29,522
"Let's have some fun tomorrow."

244
00:11:29,605 --> 00:11:30,731
How many did he give her?

245
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,026
Maybe he didn't.

246
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:35,736
He didn't.

247
00:11:36,404 --> 00:11:37,905
-He didn't?
-No.

248
00:11:40,783 --> 00:11:43,119
-Isn't it the first time he hasn't voted?
-Yeah.

249
00:11:43,202 --> 00:11:45,204
-He's trying to make it clear.
-Right.

250
00:11:45,287 --> 00:11:47,832
He must have thought we were
going to check our boxes today.

251
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:49,708
If he didn't give you any despite that…

252
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,169
Exactly. He wants me to know that

253
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,504
he didn't choose me.

254
00:11:53,587 --> 00:11:55,131
Gosh, this is giving me a headache.

255
00:11:58,801 --> 00:12:00,428
"I'll make a choice for you?"

256
00:12:00,511 --> 00:12:02,471
No, it was,
"Make the choice for yourself."

257
00:12:02,555 --> 00:12:03,764
"Make the choice for yourself."

258
00:12:03,848 --> 00:12:06,225
Then, Kyung-ho is totally into Ga-yeon.

259
00:12:06,308 --> 00:12:08,727
-But Ga-yeon gave Jung-min 163 hearts?
-Yeah.

260
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:11,814
Right. I think

261
00:12:11,897 --> 00:12:14,191
-Kyung-ho chose Ga-yeon.
-Yeah.

262
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:16,026
But Ga-yeon wants Jung-min.

263
00:12:16,110 --> 00:12:19,780
"I choose you. But you decide
for yourself." Isn't that it?

264
00:12:19,864 --> 00:12:21,574
-It could be that.
-I think you're right.

265
00:12:22,658 --> 00:12:24,493
<i>He really wanted to make it clear.</i>

266
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:28,247
Even the day before,
he gave me Heart Chips

267
00:12:28,330 --> 00:12:32,168
and said he had a good time
despite being very vague with me.

268
00:12:32,251 --> 00:12:33,669
The fact that he didn't give me any…

269
00:12:33,752 --> 00:12:37,298
He didn't even know
we weren't going to check our Heart Chips.

270
00:12:37,381 --> 00:12:39,800
so he really left
no room for interpretation.

271
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:43,888
<i>He didn't put any in my box</i>
<i>even though he thought I'd check it.</i>

272
00:12:43,971 --> 00:12:47,016
<i>And I have to spend the night with him?</i>

273
00:12:47,099 --> 00:12:50,060
I should have decided the camping thing
after talking this over.

274
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:51,270
That's why I was like, "Huh?"

275
00:12:51,353 --> 00:12:52,521
You acted too quickly.

276
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:55,065
I should've just gone
to the tent with you.

277
00:12:55,149 --> 00:12:56,525
-Can you take it back?
-No.

278
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:58,152
You did well, Do-geon.

279
00:12:58,235 --> 00:13:01,071
-If you…
-If the two of you left,

280
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:04,492
I might have joined you there.

281
00:13:05,284 --> 00:13:06,827
Like sleeping with mom and dad.

282
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:10,331
They have just changed roles with me
from yesterday.

283
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:13,042
This time, the guy is sure,
but the girl is saying,

284
00:13:13,125 --> 00:13:14,668
"I like you too

285
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:17,796
but I'm not sure yet, so please wait."

286
00:13:19,006 --> 00:13:20,966
What do we do about you?

287
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:26,764
Tell me.

288
00:13:26,847 --> 00:13:27,973
-About what?
-The notes.

289
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:30,059
-The notes?
-Yes.

290
00:13:30,142 --> 00:13:31,018
Tell me.

291
00:13:31,101 --> 00:13:31,936
Why should I?

292
00:13:32,019 --> 00:13:33,187
Tell me.

293
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:34,480
What can I do for you?

294
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:37,066
I'm curious about what the notes say.

295
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:40,444
I already know who gave me the notes.

296
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:42,279
-It's two, isn't it?
-Who?

297
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:44,156
-Kyung-ho and…
-Why do you think that?

298
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:47,701
-Because Kyung-ho told me today.
-What did he say?

299
00:13:47,785 --> 00:13:50,788
-Hmm?
-Why did he say he'd vote for you?

300
00:13:51,288 --> 00:13:53,374
He didn't say he'd vote for me.

301
00:13:53,457 --> 00:13:55,584
I think he expressed how he felt.

302
00:13:56,168 --> 00:13:57,711
-How he felt?
-Yeah.

303
00:14:00,256 --> 00:14:01,674
Hmm.

304
00:14:01,757 --> 00:14:03,008
Jung-min's message

305
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:06,262
was about how he liked you.
He said something like,

306
00:14:06,929 --> 00:14:08,639
"I'm rooting for you."

307
00:14:08,722 --> 00:14:09,640
What about Kyung-ho?

308
00:14:11,392 --> 00:14:12,351
Ask him.

309
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:16,105
He won't tell me.
I don't think he'll tell me.

310
00:14:17,356 --> 00:14:18,232
Kyung-ho.

311
00:14:19,567 --> 00:14:22,319
Congratulations on sleeping outside.

312
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:24,488
-Me?
-What did you write?

313
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:27,116
-What did I write?
-On the note.

314
00:14:27,199 --> 00:14:28,951
-Why?
-Because I'm curious.

315
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:31,662
-It's kind of cheesy to say it out loud.
-What did you write?

316
00:14:31,745 --> 00:14:32,872
I put a lot of effort into it.

317
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:35,416
That's why I'm curious.
I thought you would.

318
00:14:36,292 --> 00:14:38,502
I can't say it. I can't say it out loud.

319
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,921
-I can do it in writing.
-Yeah? Then, write it for me.

320
00:14:41,005 --> 00:14:43,591
-Okay, I'll do it later.
-Okay.

321
00:14:43,674 --> 00:14:44,842
Okay.

322
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:48,053
What did Ga-yeon ask you just now,
Your Majesty?

323
00:14:48,137 --> 00:14:51,640
-Come and have a seat here, your Majesty.
-She kept asking about her notes.

324
00:14:51,724 --> 00:14:53,475
-Oh, in her box?
-Yeah.

325
00:14:53,559 --> 00:14:54,560
Jung-min.

326
00:14:55,519 --> 00:14:56,353
What?

327
00:14:57,521 --> 00:14:59,064
What were you about to say?

328
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,566
-What was I about to say?
-Yeah.

329
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:03,027
I was just going to say,
"You got this, Jung-min."

330
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:03,944
-Really?
-Yeah.

331
00:15:08,365 --> 00:15:11,327
Ga-yeon, the king told me that I got this.

332
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:12,494
Why?

333
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:14,371
"You got this?"

334
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:18,334
What did you write?

335
00:15:19,251 --> 00:15:20,085
Me?

336
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:23,047
-I'll tell you later.
-Come on.

337
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:27,259
I really gave you a lot.

338
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:28,218
Really?

339
00:15:28,886 --> 00:15:31,347
I wanted to make you king.

340
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:33,641
So why didn't you become king?

341
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:37,227
I think the rest were determined
to make Do-geon king.

342
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:39,396
-Really?
-They conspired together.

343
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,481
Why?

344
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:44,526
I think they plotted something
just like us that one time.

345
00:15:44,610 --> 00:15:46,612
-I put most of mine in yours.
-Really?

346
00:15:46,695 --> 00:15:47,738
And

347
00:15:47,821 --> 00:15:52,326
I left a little and put most in yours.

348
00:15:52,409 --> 00:15:53,619
-Really?
-Yeah.

349
00:15:53,702 --> 00:15:57,081
What a shame. I wish I could have checked
that I had your full support.

350
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,208
I know. I thought for sure you'd be king.

351
00:15:59,291 --> 00:16:00,542
You were the only one though.

352
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:07,383
Ga-yeon must have told him
that she's still thinking about it.

353
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:08,425
Despite that,

354
00:16:09,343 --> 00:16:11,804
he only voted for her and told her
to vote the way she wants?

355
00:16:12,388 --> 00:16:14,556
Were his feelings stronger than expected?

356
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:17,184
He may be into himself for doing that.

357
00:16:17,267 --> 00:16:18,519
Do you want to have a chat with him?

358
00:16:18,602 --> 00:16:20,938
I don't even know
if there's any room for that.

359
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:25,150
If he had just told me
that's what he decided to do,

360
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:28,612
I would have accepted that.

361
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:32,116
But he just treats me like I'm invisible.

362
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:35,786
He really never looks at me.

363
00:16:35,869 --> 00:16:39,748
And they act like they are
the only two people in the world.

364
00:16:39,832 --> 00:16:41,375
-Can we pause it briefly?
-Yeah.

365
00:16:41,458 --> 00:16:42,835
Ye-rim also

366
00:16:42,918 --> 00:16:45,754
had a part in not trying hard enough.

367
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:49,633
like trying to start a conversation
with him or something.

368
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:53,220
Kyung-ho may be pleasantly surprised

369
00:16:53,303 --> 00:16:56,557
at the confident side of Ye-rim.

370
00:16:56,640 --> 00:17:01,270
She could have created opportunities
to change the atmosphere.

371
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:03,105
But she just stayed back by herself

372
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:06,692
and would just hear the opinions
of others around her.

373
00:17:06,775 --> 00:17:10,988
How could things have improved
under these circumstances?

374
00:17:11,071 --> 00:17:14,491
She keeps talking about
how he didn't make eye contact with her,

375
00:17:14,575 --> 00:17:17,119
but because she has feelings for him,

376
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:20,247
all of her attention is towards him,

377
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:21,665
so it just feels that way.

378
00:17:21,749 --> 00:17:23,751
-I've been in that exact position.
-Yeah?

379
00:17:23,834 --> 00:17:27,087
If I keep looking at him
but he never looks at me?

380
00:17:27,171 --> 00:17:29,256
Also, I'm not just anybody.

381
00:17:29,339 --> 00:17:31,175
I was someone he was into once.

382
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:35,387
So I would be very disappointed
if he didn't look at me once.

383
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:37,347
Yeah, I get that.

384
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:39,475
It's frustrating
because she reminds me of myself.

385
00:17:40,267 --> 00:17:41,769
I'm learning a life lesson from this.

386
00:17:41,852 --> 00:17:45,272
Since Kyung-ho and I are
going to talk this evening,

387
00:17:45,355 --> 00:17:46,982
<i>I was fixing my makeup.</i>

388
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,735
Even after Heart Chip votes

389
00:17:49,818 --> 00:17:51,904
and even before the announcement,

390
00:17:51,987 --> 00:17:53,405
he didn't look at me once.

391
00:17:53,489 --> 00:17:55,783
-Who wants to see the Big Dipper outside?
-Me.

392
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:57,117
-You found it?
-Yeah.

393
00:17:57,201 --> 00:17:58,368
<i>I thought it was weird.</i>

394
00:18:02,706 --> 00:18:05,334
<i>I thought we had plenty of time to talk.</i>

395
00:18:05,417 --> 00:18:07,461
-Come over here.
-Come here, Ga-yeon.

396
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:09,379
<i>But he sat next to Ga-yeon,</i>

397
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:12,382
<i>and kept making eye contact with her</i>
<i>and joking around.</i>

398
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:14,426
<i>He did it so obviously.</i>

399
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:20,057
-No, I don't want to.
-Let's have only Ga-yeon do it.

400
00:18:20,140 --> 00:18:21,350
Ga-yeon is smart.

401
00:18:21,433 --> 00:18:25,187
<i>It really felt like he was</i>
<i>treating me like I was invisible.</i>

402
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:27,231
<i>Kyung-ho used to sit next to me.</i>

403
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:29,566
Come over here.

404
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:35,614
<i>It was mostly the two of us talking then.</i>

405
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:38,909
<i>But he suddenly disappeared</i>

406
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:40,828
<i>and went over there.</i>

407
00:18:41,411 --> 00:18:43,372
<i>I felt all alone.</i>

408
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:48,669
If he wants to act natural,
he can look at me at least, right?

409
00:18:48,752 --> 00:18:50,546
That's what's so mean about him.

410
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:52,381
At first, I thought

411
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:59,054
if the two of them were happy together,
I was okay with it.

412
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:02,474
But his actions are so mean that

413
00:19:02,558 --> 00:19:04,476
I don't want them to be together.

414
00:19:06,311 --> 00:19:08,313
Tell me this one thing.

415
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:12,276
Did it turn out the way you expected
or was there anything that was surprising?

416
00:19:12,359 --> 00:19:14,528
-I kind of had an idea about most people…
-Yeah?

417
00:19:14,611 --> 00:19:16,029
…but I couldn't figure you out.

418
00:19:16,113 --> 00:19:17,239
-Really?
-Yeah.

419
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:20,409
But you can see it now, right?
I made it pretty clear.

420
00:19:20,492 --> 00:19:22,202
-Have you made up your mind now?
-I think so.

421
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:23,162
You think so?

422
00:19:23,245 --> 00:19:24,830
-I have.
-You have?

423
00:19:24,913 --> 00:19:25,914
Hmm…

424
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:27,958
Actually, Ga-yeon became my choice.

425
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:29,084
That's how I feel.

426
00:19:29,168 --> 00:19:31,044
But this is what I'm cautious about.

427
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:33,547
The date itself was so fun for me.

428
00:19:33,630 --> 00:19:35,966
I said what I wanted to say
and heard what I wanted to hear.

429
00:19:36,049 --> 00:19:39,386
And it helped me feel more at ease.

430
00:19:39,469 --> 00:19:43,390
But I'm wondering if I am
totally drawn towards Ga-yeon

431
00:19:43,473 --> 00:19:47,060
because I was briefly swayed by that
or that feeling was still lingering.

432
00:19:47,144 --> 00:19:50,063
That's why I want to think about it
one last time

433
00:19:50,147 --> 00:19:52,191
until tomorrow morning just to be safe.

434
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:53,192
Got it.

435
00:19:54,109 --> 00:19:55,777
Whose are you most curious about?

436
00:19:55,861 --> 00:19:57,321
Ga-yeon and Ye-rim's.

437
00:19:57,404 --> 00:20:00,574
First of all, Ye-rim voted for you.

438
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:03,243
She voted for you,
but she didn't give you a lot.

439
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:05,579
Why didn't she give you a lot?

440
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:07,581
She thought the king could
decide tomorrow's dates,

441
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:10,292
so she gave me over 200 hearts

442
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:12,252
-to make me king.
-Okay.

443
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:16,757
I thought Kyung-ho ought to know that.

444
00:20:16,840 --> 00:20:19,384
This is how strong
Ye-rim's feelings are towards him.

445
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:21,720
-I was surprised too.
-Right?

446
00:20:21,803 --> 00:20:24,181
I was like "She invested in me this much?"

447
00:20:24,806 --> 00:20:26,391
That's how much she likes you.

448
00:20:27,851 --> 00:20:31,647
It seemed like she has
very strong feelings for you.

449
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:34,691
But she thinks she didn't get
a chance to talk with you a lot.

450
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:35,817
That is true.

451
00:20:35,901 --> 00:20:38,362
We were both awkward
since it was the first date.

452
00:20:38,445 --> 00:20:39,655
She was really bummed about it.

453
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:42,950
-Well, she doesn't know how you feel.
-Right.

454
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:45,035
Thank you for telling me honestly.

455
00:20:45,118 --> 00:20:47,204
I definitely thought I needed to talk

456
00:20:47,287 --> 00:20:49,039
with Ye-rim, more so than Ga-yeon.

457
00:20:49,122 --> 00:20:50,040
I'll do my best to

458
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:52,376
end it well or something.

459
00:20:53,001 --> 00:20:55,254
I have to be honest no matter what.

460
00:20:55,337 --> 00:20:56,838
But that's what's so hard right now.

461
00:20:57,756 --> 00:21:00,133
I was feeling very conflicted.

462
00:21:04,137 --> 00:21:06,807
<i>I wanted to chat more with Ga-yeon too,</i>

463
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:09,601
<i>so I wanted to stay inside but…</i>

464
00:21:10,519 --> 00:21:12,145
Smell this. Doesn't it smell good?

465
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:13,063
Don't you want some?

466
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:14,564
You have to leave soon.

467
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,692
Not soon. I'll leave when it's bedtime.

468
00:21:16,775 --> 00:21:18,360
I have to wash up.

469
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:22,447
<i>It's not like I wasn't going to</i>
<i>have a conversation with Ye-rim.</i>

470
00:21:22,531 --> 00:21:25,951
<i>But it wasn't going to be</i>
<i>anything nice for her to hear.</i>

471
00:21:26,034 --> 00:21:30,664
I worried about how we were going to sleep
after saying that.

472
00:21:30,747 --> 00:21:33,166
I was going through all kinds of emotions.

473
00:21:33,250 --> 00:21:35,836
That's why I was being hesitant when…

474
00:21:38,213 --> 00:21:39,881
What time is it now?

475
00:21:39,965 --> 00:21:41,008
-Two o'clock.
-Two o'clock.

476
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:42,968
What time will you go out?

477
00:21:43,969 --> 00:21:45,137
I'm not sure.

478
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:48,473
Come on. Isn't that hurtful?
It's driving me nuts.

479
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:52,019
He looks like he's dragging his feet
because he doesn't want to go.

480
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:53,603
-Yeah.
-"Do you hate me that much?"

481
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:55,063
"Didn't you say you liked me before?"

482
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,024
How can he change his mind in a day?

483
00:21:57,107 --> 00:21:58,608
If the king decided, do as he says!

484
00:21:58,692 --> 00:21:59,735
This makes me angry.

485
00:21:59,818 --> 00:22:01,028
Wash up right now!

486
00:22:01,111 --> 00:22:02,404
What time will you go out?

487
00:22:03,530 --> 00:22:04,364
I'm not sure.

488
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:07,743
How about 2:30 a.m.?

489
00:22:07,826 --> 00:22:08,952
Go out at 2:30 a.m.?

490
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:10,871
-I can go out now.
-Really?

491
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:13,832
-Let's go out at 2:30 a.m.
-Okay.

492
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:19,796
This is making me sick.

493
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:24,926
<i>Let's just talk or maybe go back inside.</i>

494
00:22:25,010 --> 00:22:26,261
THE AGREED-UPON 2:30 A.M. CAME

495
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:33,518
Why did it have to be sleeping outside?

496
00:22:35,937 --> 00:22:37,481
What do you think about sleeping outside?

497
00:22:37,564 --> 00:22:40,150
It doesn't matter to me
whether we sleep outside or not.

498
00:22:40,233 --> 00:22:41,068
Okay.

499
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,571
I don't care if I have to.

500
00:22:44,654 --> 00:22:45,489
Okay.

501
00:22:50,702 --> 00:22:51,953
What are you eating?

502
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:53,080
It was nothing.

503
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:54,873
What?

504
00:22:56,541 --> 00:22:58,460
Is there something you want to talk about?

505
00:22:59,795 --> 00:23:01,880
Can you go…

506
00:23:02,506 --> 00:23:04,007
-Go first?
-Yeah.

507
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:07,636
It would be better for you
if I went straight to the point, right?

508
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:08,678
-No.
-No?

509
00:23:08,762 --> 00:23:09,596
No.

510
00:23:10,639 --> 00:23:14,142
How did your date go today?

511
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:15,143
It was fun.

512
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:17,729
What did you do? Foot bath?

513
00:23:17,813 --> 00:23:19,272
-Yeah, foot bath and barbecue.
-Foot bath and barbecue?

514
00:23:19,856 --> 00:23:21,608
You can't go wrong with barbecue.

515
00:23:21,691 --> 00:23:22,692
You should've asked for chicken.

516
00:23:22,776 --> 00:23:23,777
HEH

517
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:29,241
She's being prepped to be dumped.
She's facing the chopping block.

518
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:30,492
In historical dramas,

519
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:32,536
they're on their knees,
waiting to be executed.

520
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:35,455
But the executioner keeps spraying water
on his sword

521
00:23:35,539 --> 00:23:36,498
but doesn't kill him.

522
00:23:36,581 --> 00:23:38,333
It's so frustrating.

523
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:42,212
He keeps spraying water on his sword
and swings it but doesn't kill them.

524
00:23:42,295 --> 00:23:44,297
They wait for their head
to get chopped off.

525
00:23:44,381 --> 00:23:46,466
She can start the conversation though.

526
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:49,594
-This is the thing. Ye-rim likes him.
-Yeah.

527
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:52,389
-There's no scenario where she dumps him.
-Right.

528
00:23:52,472 --> 00:23:55,475
She's waiting because
Kyung-ho has to make the choice.

529
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:56,935
It's so frustrating.

530
00:23:57,018 --> 00:23:58,645
Kyung-ho frustrates me.

531
00:23:58,728 --> 00:24:00,647
Ye-rim frustrates me.

532
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:02,399
Ye-rim frustrates me too.

533
00:24:02,482 --> 00:24:04,067
Let's watch. I got worked up.

534
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:07,320
Is that what you wanted to tell me?

535
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:08,822
-What I wanted to tell you?
-Yeah.

536
00:24:09,447 --> 00:24:11,199
-No.
-I know.

537
00:24:11,283 --> 00:24:12,951
You didn't want me to get to the point.

538
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:15,579
I meant that you didn't have to
make it so brief.

539
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:22,043
I told you this yesterday.

540
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:24,671
I said I needed to
be sure about my feelings.

541
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:27,799
The thing is, I'm still unsure.

542
00:24:27,883 --> 00:24:30,802
It has only been two days since we met.

543
00:24:30,886 --> 00:24:32,470
I get that we don't have much time

544
00:24:32,554 --> 00:24:34,890
and it's too short to
get to know someone else.

545
00:24:34,973 --> 00:24:37,559
Honestly, there's someone
I am still curious about

546
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:41,521
and I don't want to feel like
I have to force myself to let go.

547
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:44,691
So I wanted to go on a date
with Ga-yeon today

548
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:45,984
and I wanted to

549
00:24:46,610 --> 00:24:48,028
sort out how I felt.

550
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:49,654
I eventually went on the date

551
00:24:49,738 --> 00:24:51,156
and I was able to

552
00:24:52,073 --> 00:24:54,201
sort it out a bit on my own.

553
00:24:54,284 --> 00:24:57,537
For today's choice, I went with Ga-yeon.

554
00:24:58,872 --> 00:24:59,915
The reason for that is

555
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:01,708
because I like

556
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:03,210
Ga-yeon…

557
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,296
more.

558
00:25:09,549 --> 00:25:10,926
That's how I feel right now.

559
00:25:15,722 --> 00:25:18,225
I don't want to be hasty by saying that

560
00:25:18,308 --> 00:25:20,352
I only have eyes for her right now.

561
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:24,147
But I am going to

562
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:26,191
make up my mind by early morning

563
00:25:27,108 --> 00:25:30,487
and that is all I can really say to you.

564
00:25:37,827 --> 00:25:41,248
It's not that I didn't expect to hear
what you just told me.

565
00:25:42,582 --> 00:25:46,878
It doesn't matter to me at all
that you chose Ga-yeon.

566
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:49,256
What I don't understand is

567
00:25:49,339 --> 00:25:51,258
the way you acted.

568
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:52,801
How did I act?

569
00:25:54,594 --> 00:25:58,932
You could have just told me.

570
00:25:59,015 --> 00:26:01,101
About what? How I felt?

571
00:26:01,184 --> 00:26:03,270
You could have just told me
what was going on.

572
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:05,021
I was really going to tell you today.

573
00:26:05,105 --> 00:26:07,190
-When?
-Within the day.

574
00:26:07,274 --> 00:26:09,567
There wasn't any time to talk
in the first place.

575
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:10,986
There was a lot of time.

576
00:26:11,736 --> 00:26:12,904
You just avoided me.

577
00:26:13,905 --> 00:26:16,658
I guess it appeared like I avoided you.

578
00:26:16,741 --> 00:26:18,410
-Yeah, I did avoid you.
-Yeah.

579
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:20,912
I could tell you were avoiding me.

580
00:26:20,996 --> 00:26:24,332
I didn't know why you had to be that way.

581
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:26,751
I thought it was a bit rude.

582
00:26:28,086 --> 00:26:31,047
I really wasn't avoiding you.

583
00:26:31,131 --> 00:26:33,758
-Really?
-I was being cautious.

584
00:26:33,842 --> 00:26:36,219
It is very hard for me to

585
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:38,680
talk about this with you.

586
00:26:38,763 --> 00:26:40,640
It's harder because it's you.

587
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:44,102
I didn't think it was a situation where
I could call you as soon as I saw you

588
00:26:44,185 --> 00:26:47,856
and say, "Let's hash it out."
At least, it wasn't like that for me.

589
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:51,401
I guess I did avoid your gaze
since I couldn't look at you.

590
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:53,653
I just feel sorry.

591
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:58,366
If you felt sorry, I don't think
you should've acted that way with Ga-yeon.

592
00:26:58,450 --> 00:27:01,619
I don't know how Ga-yeon and I acted but…

593
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:04,831
I'm getting PTSD.

594
00:27:04,914 --> 00:27:06,958
What is this?

595
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:09,502
-Kyung-ho is actually…
-It's like the show <i>EXchange</i>.

596
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:12,088
…speaking honestly right now.

597
00:27:12,672 --> 00:27:14,049
How are they supposed to sleep now?

598
00:27:14,132 --> 00:27:15,133
It would be so uncomfortable.

599
00:27:15,216 --> 00:27:17,385
Don't sleep there.
Just go to your respective beds.

600
00:27:17,469 --> 00:27:19,262
Tell the king that you can't do it.

601
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:20,347
It's up to the king.

602
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:25,310
The two of you kept exchanging
non-verbal signals to one another.

603
00:27:25,393 --> 00:27:27,312
Talking about a puppet king and whatnot.

604
00:27:27,395 --> 00:27:29,814
And you said you had a bad feeling
about sleeping outside

605
00:27:29,898 --> 00:27:31,566
and that you didn't want to do it.

606
00:27:31,649 --> 00:27:34,235
I was just going along with everyone.

607
00:27:34,319 --> 00:27:38,823
It would be weird for me to say
that I didn't care about sleeping outside.

608
00:27:38,907 --> 00:27:39,949
That's why…

609
00:27:41,868 --> 00:27:43,495
I guess you can

610
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:47,916
put meaning to everything I say and do,

611
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:49,542
but it wasn't like that for me.

612
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:50,877
Oh.

613
00:27:53,129 --> 00:27:54,339
I don't know.

614
00:27:54,839 --> 00:27:58,301
To be honest, I got a bit irritated.

615
00:27:58,385 --> 00:28:01,221
She kept dismissing everything I said.

616
00:28:01,304 --> 00:28:04,766
It seems like no matter what I say,
you can't accept it.

617
00:28:04,849 --> 00:28:07,143
I wonder if the way
I expressed myself was wrong.

618
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:09,437
I wonder if it was completely wrong.

619
00:28:10,021 --> 00:28:11,314
I really don't know.

620
00:28:11,398 --> 00:28:13,108
Think about it, Kyung-ho.

621
00:28:13,191 --> 00:28:14,109
Okay.

622
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:17,362
If you didn't have any feelings for me,

623
00:28:17,445 --> 00:28:18,613
would you have said those things?

624
00:28:18,696 --> 00:28:20,240
-To you?
-Yeah.

625
00:28:21,116 --> 00:28:22,450
<i>If it were me,</i>

626
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:24,953
<i>I wouldn't have done those things</i>
<i>if I didn't have feelings for you.</i>

627
00:28:25,495 --> 00:28:26,621
What about you?

628
00:28:27,163 --> 00:28:29,249
Would you ask me out?

629
00:28:29,332 --> 00:28:32,377
You and Ga-yeon like each other,

630
00:28:32,460 --> 00:28:34,712
but isn't Ga-yeon also curious
about Jung-min too?

631
00:28:34,796 --> 00:28:37,507
The way you feel
is the way I felt yesterday.

632
00:28:38,425 --> 00:28:42,303
Let's say Ga-yeon went on a date
with Jung-min under those circumstances.

633
00:28:43,054 --> 00:28:45,640
She starts avoiding you,

634
00:28:45,724 --> 00:28:50,603
keeps sitting next to Jung-min,
and exchanges looks with him.

635
00:28:50,687 --> 00:28:54,566
I wonder how you would react
in that situation.

636
00:28:54,649 --> 00:28:56,234
If I were in that situation,

637
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:00,822
the first thing that I would do

638
00:29:00,905 --> 00:29:03,241
is to try to do something about it.

639
00:29:03,324 --> 00:29:04,701
So what would you have done?

640
00:29:04,784 --> 00:29:06,327
I'd wonder what I did wrong

641
00:29:06,411 --> 00:29:07,871
and what I was lacking.

642
00:29:07,954 --> 00:29:09,581
-That would be the first thing
-Exactly.

643
00:29:09,664 --> 00:29:10,874
-I would do.
-Yeah.

644
00:29:10,957 --> 00:29:12,041
Can you just hear me out?

645
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:16,337
I get the feeling that
Ye-rim is trying to control Kyung-ho.

646
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:19,299
Why does she have to know
why he doesn't like her?

647
00:29:19,382 --> 00:29:22,177
That's how he feels.
He's entitled to do what he wants.

648
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:24,929
Objectively speaking,
Ye-rim is in the wrong.

649
00:29:25,013 --> 00:29:27,182
Do you know what the issue is?
The reason why she's upset?

650
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:28,975
She wasn't the one who initiated it.

651
00:29:29,058 --> 00:29:30,560
He flirted with her.

652
00:29:30,643 --> 00:29:33,438
Then, with no transition in the middle,
he just ignored her.

653
00:29:33,521 --> 00:29:35,231
It was either flirting or ignoring.

654
00:29:35,315 --> 00:29:39,277
There was no friendship or mutual respect
as a human being.

655
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:40,570
That's how she feels.

656
00:29:41,070 --> 00:29:42,363
Anyway,

657
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:45,366
one person isn't interested
and the other person is interested.

658
00:29:45,450 --> 00:29:47,327
That's why she can't be objective.

659
00:29:47,410 --> 00:29:50,830
He can see this situation objectively
since he isn't interested in her.

660
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:54,000
But Ye-rim was never able
to think objectively

661
00:29:54,083 --> 00:29:55,794
because her feelings were that big.

662
00:29:55,877 --> 00:29:56,878
This is the issue.

663
00:29:56,961 --> 00:29:58,546
I've always felt this when I had a crush.

664
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:00,965
You can't hate someone
just because you once liked them.

665
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:02,258
It can't be used as a weapon.

666
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:05,386
But if you like someone so much,
it becomes a weapon.

667
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,680
You think you can hate someone
as much as you liked them.

668
00:30:07,764 --> 00:30:09,641
-Right.
-You feel justified doing it.

669
00:30:09,724 --> 00:30:10,725
That's really bad though.

670
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:13,019
Yeah,
that's what drives the other person crazy.

671
00:30:13,102 --> 00:30:15,897
Exactly. But you can only fix it
when you go through it yourself.

672
00:30:15,980 --> 00:30:17,899
I think Ye-rim will also regret it
when she sees this.

673
00:30:17,982 --> 00:30:21,069
-My heart was aching because…
-Ye-rim.

674
00:30:21,152 --> 00:30:23,196
…she's doing exactly what I did.

675
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:24,447
I feel so uncomfortable.

676
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:26,199
This is going to be a hit.

677
00:30:27,909 --> 00:30:29,577
I think I would've tried harder.

678
00:30:37,335 --> 00:30:39,212
How would I know?

679
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:40,713
But…

680
00:30:44,759 --> 00:30:45,844
if it were me,

681
00:30:49,097 --> 00:30:50,348
I wouldn't have given up.

682
00:30:50,431 --> 00:30:51,307
But

683
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:54,519
I wouldn't want to burden them either.

684
00:30:56,271 --> 00:30:57,272
That's it.

685
00:30:58,231 --> 00:30:59,357
I see.

686
00:31:01,442 --> 00:31:05,780
In my case,
regardless of giving up or not,

687
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:10,952
I think I would have been
disappointed by their actions.

688
00:31:11,578 --> 00:31:13,621
Of course, I can't be a good person to you

689
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:16,457
since I didn't act the way you wanted.

690
00:31:16,541 --> 00:31:19,127
I don't know how many things
you don't understand.

691
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:21,421
No, I do understand.

692
00:31:21,504 --> 00:31:23,423
I understand it from your perspective.

693
00:31:23,506 --> 00:31:25,133
Then, what do you want to tell me?

694
00:31:25,216 --> 00:31:27,969
You understand me but you're disappointed.
Is that it?

695
00:31:28,052 --> 00:31:30,054
I understand you,
but what you did was bad.

696
00:31:30,138 --> 00:31:32,390
I had no choice but to act badly.

697
00:31:32,473 --> 00:31:35,101
But no matter how nice I was to you,

698
00:31:35,852 --> 00:31:37,729
-I would've seemed bad to you.
-Sure.

699
00:31:38,938 --> 00:31:40,607
What is it now?

700
00:31:40,690 --> 00:31:44,569
I really hate it when someone
speaks to me in a sarcastic tone.

701
00:31:44,652 --> 00:31:47,614
So I wondered if she was talking to me
like that to provoke me

702
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:51,117
or it felt that way to me
because I was too sensitive.

703
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:53,369
Why? What is it?

704
00:31:54,203 --> 00:31:56,247
How do you want me to say it?

705
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:57,916
Hmm?

706
00:32:04,589 --> 00:32:05,757
But did I really

707
00:32:06,883 --> 00:32:08,051
act so irresponsibly?

708
00:32:08,134 --> 00:32:10,053
As I told you yesterday,

709
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:12,764
I didn't want to give an uncertain answer

710
00:32:12,847 --> 00:32:15,099
and that's why I needed time.

711
00:32:15,183 --> 00:32:18,144
And I should be the one
to decide that time

712
00:32:18,227 --> 00:32:20,271
since I was the one that needed time.

713
00:32:21,230 --> 00:32:22,440
I didn't forget about it

714
00:32:22,523 --> 00:32:24,984
and I was definitely going to tell you.

715
00:32:25,568 --> 00:32:27,987
I just needed some time to prepare.

716
00:32:30,448 --> 00:32:34,410
Why are you so hesitant
to bring that up to me?

717
00:32:34,911 --> 00:32:35,995
Of course, I should be.

718
00:32:37,914 --> 00:32:40,166
-Shouldn't I?
-But I don't know what you're thinking.

719
00:32:42,794 --> 00:32:45,046
You were really my first choice.

720
00:32:45,129 --> 00:32:48,049
I guess I believed that

721
00:32:48,132 --> 00:32:52,804
our relationship was difficult
to walk away from.

722
00:32:54,722 --> 00:32:56,182
That's why I did that.

723
00:32:58,184 --> 00:32:59,060
Okay.

724
00:33:02,897 --> 00:33:04,899
You have nothing more to say, right?

725
00:33:04,983 --> 00:33:06,234
-Me?
-Yeah.

726
00:33:06,317 --> 00:33:07,944
I am really

727
00:33:09,612 --> 00:33:11,197
sorry that I acted that way.

728
00:33:13,783 --> 00:33:15,118
I have nothing else.

729
00:33:16,285 --> 00:33:17,328
Me neither.

730
00:33:25,837 --> 00:33:27,380
<i>I want to go on a date tomorrow.</i>

731
00:33:27,463 --> 00:33:29,549
We haven't been able to

732
00:33:30,425 --> 00:33:31,926
have a conversation yet.

733
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:34,012
-Didn't we talk a lot?
-Well…

734
00:33:34,095 --> 00:33:35,471
-A heartfelt one?
-Yeah.

735
00:33:35,555 --> 00:33:36,389
We haven't had that.

736
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:39,183
-We held hands in front of the fireplace.
-Not that.

737
00:33:39,267 --> 00:33:40,435
We talked while starting the fire.

738
00:33:41,019 --> 00:33:42,520
"Fire."

739
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:44,731
Something more…

740
00:33:45,398 --> 00:33:46,566
-More meaningful?
-Yeah.

741
00:33:47,150 --> 00:33:48,484
-Shall we go to bed at 3 a.m.?
-Okay.

742
00:33:48,568 --> 00:33:50,403
Let me see this.

743
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:53,865
It's not good to wear
a bandage for too long.

744
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:57,118
Come on. This is nothing, right?

745
00:33:57,201 --> 00:33:58,202
I'm a man.

746
00:34:06,335 --> 00:34:07,670
Let's be friends.

747
00:34:12,633 --> 00:34:13,634
Why are you laughing?

748
00:34:14,761 --> 00:34:15,720
Okay.

749
00:34:17,847 --> 00:34:18,848
Thanks.

750
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:24,395
I think I'm going to cry.

751
00:34:24,479 --> 00:34:27,190
"Let's be friends" must be

752
00:34:27,273 --> 00:34:30,109
the most absurd thing ever for Kyung-ho.

753
00:34:33,446 --> 00:34:34,697
Let's be friends?

754
00:34:35,281 --> 00:34:37,825
After tormenting me emotionally?

755
00:34:38,451 --> 00:34:39,660
That's probably what

756
00:34:41,454 --> 00:34:42,455
Kyung-ho is thinking.

757
00:34:42,538 --> 00:34:43,706
I'm gonna cry.

758
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:44,665
I'm serious.

759
00:34:45,833 --> 00:34:49,087
Ye-rim must have had
so many thoughts from there.

760
00:34:49,170 --> 00:34:50,880
-I'm sure.
-So many thoughts.

761
00:34:50,963 --> 00:34:52,757
I'm sure it won't be easy to be friends.

762
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:56,052
I mean, she probably felt sorry
and felt like she reacted immaturely,

763
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:58,012
so she wanted to make things less awkward.

764
00:34:58,096 --> 00:35:00,431
That's why she just said that.

765
00:35:00,515 --> 00:35:02,016
She should've said sorry sooner.

766
00:35:02,600 --> 00:35:04,560
I don't want to be friends with you.

767
00:35:04,644 --> 00:35:06,479
Kyung-ho said sorry.

768
00:35:06,562 --> 00:35:08,523
Why should Ye-rim feel so sorry?

769
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:14,987
Ye-rim viewed things emotionally
only in the way she wanted.

770
00:35:15,613 --> 00:35:17,573
I understand how she feels,

771
00:35:17,657 --> 00:35:19,826
but I understand how Kyung-ho feels too.

772
00:35:19,909 --> 00:35:23,287
If Kyung-ho apologized,
Ye-rim should apologize too.

773
00:35:23,371 --> 00:35:25,039
It was

774
00:35:25,873 --> 00:35:29,168
a very clumsy expression of her feelings
when she said, "Let's be friends."

775
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:31,921
-Hold on.
-This is unbelievable.

776
00:35:33,840 --> 00:35:35,424
-It's just that…
-Yeah?

777
00:35:35,508 --> 00:35:37,468
…I got too immersed in this. Oh, no.

778
00:35:37,552 --> 00:35:38,845
Seriously though,

779
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:40,555
-I was in a similar situation.
-Yeah?

780
00:35:40,638 --> 00:35:41,722
But I was also…

781
00:35:46,602 --> 00:35:47,562
I guess I'm not over it.

782
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:51,774
I made a situation worse like her once.

783
00:35:51,858 --> 00:35:53,651
I interpreted things so badly.

784
00:35:53,734 --> 00:35:54,986
I read into things too much.

785
00:35:55,069 --> 00:35:57,363
When the mood got really tense,

786
00:35:57,446 --> 00:35:58,948
I said something like that too.

787
00:35:59,532 --> 00:36:01,868
I just said,
"Let's make up and be friends."

788
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:03,077
Just like her.

789
00:36:03,161 --> 00:36:03,995
I tried…

790
00:36:04,078 --> 00:36:08,082
You see, my friends would take my side
when I criticize the person I liked.

791
00:36:08,166 --> 00:36:11,085
Even though they knew I was wrong,
they would all take my side.

792
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:14,088
So I ended up really hating that person,

793
00:36:14,172 --> 00:36:16,632
but when Joo-heon explained
how he must have felt,

794
00:36:16,716 --> 00:36:18,968
I thought of my own mistakes

795
00:36:19,051 --> 00:36:20,803
and felt so bad all of a sudden.

796
00:36:21,470 --> 00:36:23,431
I saw so much of myself in Ye-rim.

797
00:36:23,514 --> 00:36:27,310
There's one more thing that I want to say.

798
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:32,690
Kyung-ho wasn't someone
who could handle a woman like Ye-rim.

799
00:36:32,773 --> 00:36:34,942
Two people with the same capacity

800
00:36:35,026 --> 00:36:38,613
-can't make room for each other.
-Unbelievable.

801
00:36:38,696 --> 00:36:43,075
But someone with a bigger capacity
can always make room for the smaller.

802
00:36:43,159 --> 00:36:45,953
When Ye-rim acts that way,

803
00:36:46,037 --> 00:36:48,998
she needs to meet someone
who can embrace her.

804
00:36:49,582 --> 00:36:51,209
The same applies for you too.

805
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:54,086
That person didn't have the capacity
to handle you.

806
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:57,423
I hope they don't get the wrong idea.
There were many guys that I liked.

807
00:36:59,508 --> 00:37:02,094
-That's why--
-How many were there?

808
00:37:02,178 --> 00:37:04,388
-I don't want anyone to get it wrong.
-How many were there?

809
00:37:04,472 --> 00:37:07,141
I don't want them to think
that I was crying because of them.

810
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:09,101
It isn't anyone recent.

811
00:37:10,311 --> 00:37:11,854
It's not from this year.

812
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:13,731
It isn't the recent person
you said you met?

813
00:37:13,814 --> 00:37:15,149
-Oh, not him?
-No, before him.

814
00:37:17,568 --> 00:37:19,862
Gosh, this is new.

815
00:37:20,446 --> 00:37:22,615
After I got back from the date,

816
00:37:22,698 --> 00:37:25,326
it was nice when I was just with Jung-min,

817
00:37:25,409 --> 00:37:26,869
without Kyung-ho around.

818
00:37:26,953 --> 00:37:28,037
Of course.

819
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:30,539
But if you were with Jung-min?

820
00:37:30,623 --> 00:37:32,208
You'd miss Kyung-ho.

821
00:37:32,291 --> 00:37:33,125
Yeah.

822
00:37:33,209 --> 00:37:35,419
Jung-min is the safe choice.

823
00:37:35,503 --> 00:37:38,589
But the excitement
and the strong attraction

824
00:37:38,673 --> 00:37:40,341
is Kyung-ho.

825
00:37:44,303 --> 00:37:45,972
It isn't that I don't like Jung-min.

826
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:48,307
It's different. You see…

827
00:38:07,994 --> 00:38:09,870
I'll head out first.

828
00:38:15,793 --> 00:38:17,169
<i>What do I do now?</i>

829
00:38:18,254 --> 00:38:21,590
Did you sleep well, Ye-rim?
It must've been so uncomfortable.

830
00:38:21,674 --> 00:38:24,093
He slept so well next to me though.

831
00:38:24,885 --> 00:38:26,387
<i>After talking so much with him,</i>

832
00:38:26,470 --> 00:38:30,224
<i>I didn't want to try to</i>
<i>make a move on Kyung-ho anymore.</i>

833
00:38:31,350 --> 00:38:32,768
You look good together.

834
00:38:34,312 --> 00:38:36,314
-Do this pose.
-What?

835
00:38:36,397 --> 00:38:38,316
<i>If I had to choose,</i>
<i>Do-geon's my second choice.</i>

836
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:42,695
<i>But I didn't want to take</i>
<i>the time away from those two either.</i>

837
00:38:46,032 --> 00:38:48,909
<i>Then, what am I supposed to do now?</i>

838
00:39:05,009 --> 00:39:06,260
-Is it a devil?
-Yeah.

839
00:39:09,221 --> 00:39:11,515
-How was it in the tent?
-The tent?

840
00:39:11,599 --> 00:39:13,851
There isn't much to say.

841
00:39:13,934 --> 00:39:15,519
I fell asleep before I even knew it.

842
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:17,229
I was so tired.

843
00:39:20,232 --> 00:39:21,317
Did you eat anything?

844
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,860
Yeah, I had a sandwich.

845
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:27,490
So this morning,
Jung-min was lying on the couch

846
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:30,076
while Kyung-ho was seated and drawing.

847
00:39:30,951 --> 00:39:32,870
I felt my body leading me one way.

848
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:33,829
Of course.

849
00:39:33,913 --> 00:39:36,248
-My head was going towards Jung-min.
-Of course, it's different.

850
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:38,417
I think you should go for Kyung-ho.

851
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:41,462
-You were leaning…
-I can't be like this.

852
00:39:41,545 --> 00:39:43,089
There's nothing you can't be.

853
00:39:43,172 --> 00:39:45,966
Dating someone like Jung-min
is the right choice.

854
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:49,345
But my eyes keep drifting toward Kyung-ho.

855
00:39:49,428 --> 00:39:50,930
-I'm drawn to him.
-Yeah.

856
00:39:51,013 --> 00:39:53,140
-My body just goes to him.
-Of course.

857
00:39:53,224 --> 00:39:54,725
He's handsome.

858
00:39:57,061 --> 00:39:58,437
Gosh.

859
00:39:58,521 --> 00:40:00,231
My head hurts.

860
00:40:00,314 --> 00:40:02,900
Why must I endure such hardship?

861
00:40:02,983 --> 00:40:03,943
It's a good thing

862
00:40:04,026 --> 00:40:06,404
since it means you're popular.

863
00:40:06,904 --> 00:40:08,197
Did you sleep well?

864
00:40:09,532 --> 00:40:11,784
-I have so much on my mind.
-Why?

865
00:40:11,867 --> 00:40:14,036
My eyes keep drifting toward Kyung-ho.

866
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:15,496
It's like--

867
00:40:15,579 --> 00:40:17,623
If I were you, I wouldn't change my mind.

868
00:40:18,749 --> 00:40:21,877
This comes down to
a difference in people's personalities,

869
00:40:21,961 --> 00:40:24,588
so it's hard to suggest
a direction for you.

870
00:40:24,672 --> 00:40:29,009
In the beginning,
I only had romantic feelings for Jung-min.

871
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:34,473
But Kyung-ho is the one that
draws my attention.

872
00:40:34,557 --> 00:40:37,226
You don't know why
but you're drawn to him?

873
00:40:37,309 --> 00:40:39,353
I don't know why. I'm just drawn to him.

874
00:40:39,937 --> 00:40:41,939
Our eyes met so many times,

875
00:40:42,022 --> 00:40:43,524
so I asked him

876
00:40:43,607 --> 00:40:45,234
if he usually looks at people like that.

877
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:47,570
Kyung-ho makes proper eye contact.

878
00:40:47,653 --> 00:40:49,989
-Right?
-I think he's just like that.

879
00:40:50,072 --> 00:40:52,908
I thought I made a lot of
eye contact with him too,

880
00:40:52,992 --> 00:40:55,453
so I honestly had the wrong idea.

881
00:40:57,371 --> 00:40:59,582
It's a bit embarrassing to say,

882
00:40:59,665 --> 00:41:02,418
but I thought he was interested in me.

883
00:41:02,501 --> 00:41:03,836
He looks at people like that.

884
00:41:03,919 --> 00:41:05,671
-He gazes at you.
-With depth.

885
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:07,131
I feel captivated.

886
00:41:07,214 --> 00:41:08,466
Look at Do-geon.

887
00:41:08,549 --> 00:41:10,384
-I feel at ease.
-Look at Do-geon.

888
00:41:10,968 --> 00:41:12,470
Me too.

889
00:41:12,553 --> 00:41:14,263
HE WAS JUST EATING HIS CUP NOODLES

890
00:41:14,346 --> 00:41:17,266
I had no interest in Jung-min.
In fact, I was more interested in Do-geon.

891
00:41:17,349 --> 00:41:18,684
Do-geon and Kyung-ho.

892
00:41:18,767 --> 00:41:21,187
But holding hands played a huge part.

893
00:41:22,521 --> 00:41:23,939
I haven't experienced that.

894
00:41:28,068 --> 00:41:29,737
Am I in denial right now?

895
00:41:29,820 --> 00:41:30,779
Of course.

896
00:41:30,863 --> 00:41:32,656
That's why you're more drawn to him.

897
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:36,035
You'd feel sorry for some people
if you chose Kyung-ho.

898
00:41:36,118 --> 00:41:38,454
-Jung-min and Ye-rim.
-Maybe you can't make up your mind

899
00:41:38,537 --> 00:41:39,997
because of that.

900
00:41:40,915 --> 00:41:43,792
<i>I have a lot on my mind right now.</i>

901
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:47,046
The two men are so different.

902
00:41:47,129 --> 00:41:48,214
It's so hard

903
00:41:48,297 --> 00:41:50,466
and I don't know
how I feel exactly either.

904
00:42:03,521 --> 00:42:04,730
<i>We must've gotten something.</i>

905
00:42:06,065 --> 00:42:07,358
THE SECRET DATE BEGINS NOW

906
00:42:07,441 --> 00:42:10,694
YOUR DATE AND YOUR DESTINATION IS A SECRET
EVERYONE MUST LEAVE NOW

907
00:42:10,778 --> 00:42:13,197
"Tomorrow is the day
for secret conversations."

908
00:42:13,280 --> 00:42:15,199
"You'll have the chance to secretly have

909
00:42:15,282 --> 00:42:17,868
a one-on-one conversation with
the person you're interested in."

910
00:42:17,952 --> 00:42:20,287
"Text the person's name you'd like to have

911
00:42:20,371 --> 00:42:22,248
a secret conversation with tomorrow."

912
00:42:22,331 --> 00:42:24,542
"You can request up to
two people of the opposite sex."

913
00:42:24,625 --> 00:42:25,793
Up to two people?

914
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:27,002
Gosh.

915
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:29,922
<i>I had more questions to ask him.</i>

916
00:42:30,005 --> 00:42:32,049
<i>Why does he want to choose me?</i>

917
00:42:32,132 --> 00:42:36,845
I was hoping it wasn't simply because
I was the first person he spoke to.

918
00:42:37,429 --> 00:42:39,139
<i>Through the secret conversations,</i>

919
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:42,977
I wanted to confirm my feelings
for Jung-min and Kyung-ho.

920
00:42:43,060 --> 00:42:46,564
<i>I needed to talk to Ga-yeon</i>
<i>since we may not get to go on a date.</i>

921
00:42:46,647 --> 00:42:49,900
Rather than having a secret conversation,
I think we'll just go out on a date.

922
00:42:49,984 --> 00:42:51,944
<i>Do you know where we have to go?</i>

923
00:42:53,612 --> 00:42:56,156
CAFE BONJOUR
SECRET DATE

924
00:43:03,747 --> 00:43:04,582
Huh?

925
00:43:04,665 --> 00:43:05,874
This place looks familiar.

926
00:43:07,501 --> 00:43:09,753
Didn't the bad picture-taking two
take pictures here?

927
00:43:09,837 --> 00:43:10,963
You're right!

928
00:43:11,046 --> 00:43:13,424
Are you reusing previous locations?
Come on!

929
00:43:13,507 --> 00:43:15,759
Yeah, the two that were
bad at taking photos.

930
00:43:29,481 --> 00:43:30,983
You scared me!

931
00:43:31,066 --> 00:43:32,192
CHAE-RIN AND DO-GEON
SECRET DATE

932
00:43:32,276 --> 00:43:33,652
I was so startled.

933
00:43:33,736 --> 00:43:34,778
When did you get here?

934
00:43:34,862 --> 00:43:36,822
Maybe about five minutes ago?

935
00:43:37,781 --> 00:43:39,158
Anything you want to ask me?

936
00:43:39,241 --> 00:43:41,535
I want to know
who you're going to see today.

937
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:42,911
That's what you want to know?

938
00:43:42,995 --> 00:43:44,913
Of course. You aren't curious about that?

939
00:43:44,997 --> 00:43:46,457
I'm curious too.

940
00:43:46,540 --> 00:43:47,458
Really?

941
00:43:48,125 --> 00:43:49,126
I'm not going to tell you.

942
00:43:50,210 --> 00:43:51,629
-Did you request two people?
-What?

943
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:53,547
What?

944
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:56,300
Who knows?
I may have requested two people.

945
00:43:56,967 --> 00:43:59,803
You said you had a second choice.

946
00:43:59,887 --> 00:44:01,180
You were curious about two.

947
00:44:01,263 --> 00:44:02,640
I don't know who that is.

948
00:44:02,723 --> 00:44:04,058
Do you want to know?

949
00:44:04,141 --> 00:44:05,142
Of course I would.

950
00:44:05,225 --> 00:44:06,435
-Are you curious?
-Yeah.

951
00:44:06,518 --> 00:44:08,312
Actually, I knew who it was.

952
00:44:08,812 --> 00:44:11,774
But I wanted to hear it directly from him.

953
00:44:11,857 --> 00:44:13,233
When I asked him who it was…

954
00:44:13,317 --> 00:44:14,818
It was Ga-yeon.

955
00:44:16,153 --> 00:44:18,781
So I talked to her.

956
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:22,868
Were you able to make up your mind
after talking to her?

957
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:24,536
Yeah.

958
00:44:24,620 --> 00:44:28,415
-And you sat next to me on the first day.
-Yeah.

959
00:44:28,499 --> 00:44:30,918
-We talked quite a bit, didn't we?
-Yeah.

960
00:44:31,001 --> 00:44:32,878
<i>Since then, I thought,</i>

961
00:44:32,961 --> 00:44:35,422
<i>"This person is funny."</i>

962
00:44:35,506 --> 00:44:37,925
On the first day, people said that

963
00:44:38,008 --> 00:44:42,680
you chose me because we sat
next to each other for a long time

964
00:44:42,763 --> 00:44:44,848
in the beginning.

965
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:47,726
THE FIRST DAY, AFTER CHOOSING DATES

966
00:44:47,810 --> 00:44:49,520
I think I know why he chose her.

967
00:44:49,603 --> 00:44:51,855
-The two of you talked the most.
-Yeah.

968
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:53,399
They stayed next to each other.

969
00:44:53,482 --> 00:44:55,234
I think all of that is true.

970
00:44:55,818 --> 00:44:57,486
<i>I was a bit disappointed by that.</i>

971
00:44:57,569 --> 00:44:59,655
If that was really true,

972
00:44:59,738 --> 00:45:02,783
I wouldn't be his first choice

973
00:45:02,866 --> 00:45:06,453
if someone else sat next to him
in the beginning.

974
00:45:06,537 --> 00:45:09,039
Did you choose me as a safe choice

975
00:45:09,873 --> 00:45:12,709
because I was the first person
you spoke to?

976
00:45:13,502 --> 00:45:15,421
I started having that thought.

977
00:45:16,004 --> 00:45:19,716
I wouldn't have kept talking with you
if I wasn't interested in you.

978
00:45:21,343 --> 00:45:22,678
Don't you think so?

979
00:45:22,761 --> 00:45:26,098
If people were to get paired up
just by sitting next to each other,

980
00:45:26,181 --> 00:45:28,225
everything should've been decided there.

981
00:45:28,308 --> 00:45:30,811
Everyone should have been
paired up with the person next to them.

982
00:45:30,894 --> 00:45:32,938
I think it ended up this way
because it was you.

983
00:45:33,730 --> 00:45:36,358
What do you like about me?

984
00:45:36,442 --> 00:45:37,651
I like your personality

985
00:45:39,027 --> 00:45:40,863
and your appearance

986
00:45:41,447 --> 00:45:42,948
matches my ideal type.

987
00:45:44,199 --> 00:45:45,242
I see.

988
00:45:45,325 --> 00:45:47,411
He said it reassuringly,

989
00:45:47,494 --> 00:45:49,997
so I was satisfied.

990
00:45:51,123 --> 00:45:54,209
Let me ask you. Why was it me?

991
00:45:54,293 --> 00:45:55,878
-You?
-I'm curious.

992
00:45:55,961 --> 00:45:57,129
-Are you curious?
-Yeah.

993
00:45:57,212 --> 00:45:58,255
<i>Now</i> you're curious?

994
00:45:59,882 --> 00:46:04,011
When I first saw you,
you were close to my ideal type.

995
00:46:05,554 --> 00:46:08,474
And when we got to talking,
it seemed like we clicked.

996
00:46:08,557 --> 00:46:11,268
You're calm but subtly funny.

997
00:46:11,351 --> 00:46:12,561
I like that about you.

998
00:46:13,061 --> 00:46:15,856
I like that you aren't over the top.

999
00:46:15,939 --> 00:46:19,276
You said that you don't view
younger guys as men.

1000
00:46:20,861 --> 00:46:24,698
I've never viewed younger guys as men.

1001
00:46:26,158 --> 00:46:27,159
You remember that?

1002
00:46:27,242 --> 00:46:28,660
-Of course.
-Thanks.

1003
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:29,953
It left an impression on me.

1004
00:46:30,996 --> 00:46:32,331
It left the strongest impression.

1005
00:46:33,081 --> 00:46:35,709
-The strongest impression?
-She doesn't view younger guys as men?

1006
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:37,753
How did you feel after hearing that?

1007
00:46:37,836 --> 00:46:39,338
I didn't think much about it.

1008
00:46:39,421 --> 00:46:40,464
Why not?

1009
00:46:41,006 --> 00:46:42,299
-You were confident?
-I was confident.

1010
00:46:45,844 --> 00:46:47,221
Do you still not view me as a man?

1011
00:46:48,138 --> 00:46:50,015
-I thought you were confident.
-I am confident.

1012
00:46:50,599 --> 00:46:52,142
I just want to know what you think.

1013
00:46:53,268 --> 00:46:55,646
I'm at about "Maybe he's not that bad."

1014
00:46:55,729 --> 00:46:57,022
I'm keeping the door open.

1015
00:46:58,315 --> 00:46:59,149
I see.

1016
00:46:59,233 --> 00:47:01,109
<i>I had a very good time.</i>

1017
00:47:01,652 --> 00:47:04,863
I feel at ease when I'm with her

1018
00:47:04,947 --> 00:47:07,074
and we communicate well.

1019
00:47:07,741 --> 00:47:11,370
I think those aspects
are what make us compatible.

1020
00:47:11,453 --> 00:47:15,249
I really felt that our feelings

1021
00:47:15,332 --> 00:47:17,125
were mutual.

1022
00:47:18,460 --> 00:47:19,628
See you later.

1023
00:47:19,711 --> 00:47:20,921
CHAE-RIN AND DO-GEON
SECRET DATE ENDS

1024
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,840
CAFE MOMENT OF MOMENTS
SECRET DATE

1025
00:47:47,614 --> 00:47:48,782
He's here.

1026
00:47:52,911 --> 00:47:55,080
-Why did you come so late?
-Did I keep you waiting?

1027
00:47:55,163 --> 00:47:56,707
-Yeah.
-What were you doing?

1028
00:47:56,790 --> 00:47:57,791
Just waiting.

1029
00:47:57,874 --> 00:47:59,001
Really?

1030
00:47:59,084 --> 00:48:00,711
The conversations we have

1031
00:48:00,794 --> 00:48:04,298
back at the house
and outside are so different.

1032
00:48:04,381 --> 00:48:07,175
Not only can I focus on you completely,

1033
00:48:08,010 --> 00:48:09,344
I also feel more at ease…

1034
00:48:09,428 --> 00:48:10,971
-Really?
-…when I'm with you.

1035
00:48:11,054 --> 00:48:13,223
When it's just the two of us…

1036
00:48:13,307 --> 00:48:14,349
Do you feel calm?

1037
00:48:14,433 --> 00:48:15,642
-I feel calm.
-And?

1038
00:48:15,726 --> 00:48:18,353
-I don't feel like I have to try.
-Yeah?

1039
00:48:18,937 --> 00:48:21,857
Is how you are around me
close to how you are normally?

1040
00:48:22,441 --> 00:48:25,235
It feels like the way I am
when I am truly by myself.

1041
00:48:25,319 --> 00:48:27,112
-It feels similar to that?
-Yeah.

1042
00:48:27,195 --> 00:48:28,030
Really?

1043
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:31,450
<i>When I look into his eyes,</i>

1044
00:48:31,533 --> 00:48:34,578
<i>they look so kind and pure.</i>

1045
00:48:34,661 --> 00:48:36,121
But he's smart too.

1046
00:48:36,204 --> 00:48:37,539
He's very different from me.

1047
00:48:37,623 --> 00:48:42,252
My father made a list of rules for me.

1048
00:48:42,336 --> 00:48:43,629
One,

1049
00:48:43,712 --> 00:48:46,214
don't show your ignorance.

1050
00:48:46,298 --> 00:48:48,342
Two, since I cough a lot,

1051
00:48:48,425 --> 00:48:52,304
either do it quietly
or go to the bathroom and do it.

1052
00:48:52,387 --> 00:48:53,680
And three,

1053
00:48:55,724 --> 00:48:58,393
don't go around farting everywhere.

1054
00:49:00,395 --> 00:49:02,064
It fascinates me that

1055
00:49:02,648 --> 00:49:06,777
I met someone who is close to

1056
00:49:07,402 --> 00:49:09,613
my ideal type.

1057
00:49:12,282 --> 00:49:13,575
Don't think too much about it.

1058
00:49:13,659 --> 00:49:14,701
Just

1059
00:49:15,869 --> 00:49:17,245
accept it for what it is.

1060
00:49:18,205 --> 00:49:19,331
There's nothing to dwell on.

1061
00:49:21,124 --> 00:49:22,250
I'm serious.

1062
00:49:22,334 --> 00:49:23,377
Want to go see the ocean?

1063
00:49:24,753 --> 00:49:28,131
Regardless of the secret date,
it's the day before the final decision,

1064
00:49:28,215 --> 00:49:29,716
so I wanted to reassure her

1065
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:32,427
of my feelings for her
and that I'll choose her tomorrow.

1066
00:49:32,511 --> 00:49:34,888
Ha-yoon calmly expresses

1067
00:49:34,971 --> 00:49:37,265
how he feels about me.

1068
00:49:37,349 --> 00:49:39,434
He isn't the kind of person

1069
00:49:39,518 --> 00:49:42,437
who wants me to open up to him right away.

1070
00:49:42,521 --> 00:49:44,940
So when he occasionally reassures me,

1071
00:49:45,023 --> 00:49:49,361
I think I am able to open up to him
little by little.

1072
00:49:49,444 --> 00:49:50,696
HYE-WON AND HA-YOON
SECRET DATE ENDS

1073
00:49:50,779 --> 00:49:52,489
-I'll get going.
-See you.

1074
00:49:52,572 --> 00:49:53,490
-Bye.
-Bye.

1075
00:50:05,794 --> 00:50:06,962
What?

1076
00:50:07,295 --> 00:50:08,839
HEADS THE WRONG WAY FROM THE DOOR

1077
00:50:11,842 --> 00:50:13,385
BACKTRACKS

1078
00:50:13,468 --> 00:50:14,428
What's going on?

1079
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:17,931
-What's going on?
-What?

1080
00:50:18,557 --> 00:50:20,475
-I had no idea.
-About what?

1081
00:50:21,059 --> 00:50:22,978
-You requested a secret date with me?
-Yes.

1082
00:50:23,061 --> 00:50:24,187
Why?

1083
00:50:24,271 --> 00:50:25,605
I wanted to have a chat with you.

1084
00:50:25,689 --> 00:50:26,815
-Really?
-Yeah.

1085
00:50:26,898 --> 00:50:28,150
We can choose two people, right?

1086
00:50:28,233 --> 00:50:29,985
Isn't it up to two people?

1087
00:50:30,068 --> 00:50:31,403
-Really?
-Yeah.

1088
00:50:31,486 --> 00:50:34,281
I thought we had to choose two people.

1089
00:50:34,364 --> 00:50:35,824
I chose her because we are the same age

1090
00:50:35,907 --> 00:50:38,827
<i>and I wanted to ask her about things</i>
<i>I was curious about.</i>

1091
00:50:38,910 --> 00:50:40,996
When you were the queen,

1092
00:50:41,079 --> 00:50:43,582
why did you pair us up like that?

1093
00:50:45,625 --> 00:50:47,210
Why did you do that?

1094
00:50:47,294 --> 00:50:48,670
<i>I gave hearts to Hye-won.</i>

1095
00:50:48,754 --> 00:50:50,797
GAVE HER A LOT OF HEART CHIPS
TO MAKE HYE-WON KING

1096
00:50:50,881 --> 00:50:52,716
Ga-yeon and Kyung-ho.

1097
00:50:52,799 --> 00:50:54,134
BUT SHE BETRAYED HIM

1098
00:50:54,217 --> 00:50:57,012
I felt like everyone had to spray out.

1099
00:50:57,888 --> 00:51:00,557
You could spend some time
away from Ga-yeon

1100
00:51:01,141 --> 00:51:02,934
and see if you really got jealous.

1101
00:51:03,977 --> 00:51:07,063
-To figure that out.
-Really? You thought of all that?

1102
00:51:07,147 --> 00:51:08,607
Yeah, I thought of all that.

1103
00:51:08,690 --> 00:51:10,108
-And…
-Yeah?

1104
00:51:10,192 --> 00:51:12,527
…I thought you and Chae-rin
were a good match.

1105
00:51:13,528 --> 00:51:16,072
The queen had a vision in mind.

1106
00:51:16,156 --> 00:51:17,407
That's why…

1107
00:51:17,491 --> 00:51:19,868
<i>I thought she would feel sorry.</i>

1108
00:51:19,951 --> 00:51:21,161
If she felt sorry,

1109
00:51:21,244 --> 00:51:23,205
I was going to tell her not to be sorry

1110
00:51:23,288 --> 00:51:25,373
and that I rather enjoyed it.

1111
00:51:25,457 --> 00:51:27,793
<i>But she wasn't sorry,</i>
<i>so I didn't mention it.</i>

1112
00:51:29,169 --> 00:51:30,504
How do you feel?

1113
00:51:30,587 --> 00:51:31,838
It's Ga-yeon for me.

1114
00:51:31,922 --> 00:51:33,256
I know.

1115
00:51:33,840 --> 00:51:36,301
Try to see what's on her mind later.

1116
00:51:36,384 --> 00:51:37,677
-What?
-Ga-yeon.

1117
00:51:38,261 --> 00:51:40,055
"How do you feel, Ga-yeon?"

1118
00:51:40,138 --> 00:51:42,098
"Do you feel the same still?"

1119
00:51:42,182 --> 00:51:43,350
Things like that.

1120
00:51:44,601 --> 00:51:46,895
-I didn't prepare this--
-You came here to tell me this.

1121
00:51:46,978 --> 00:51:49,648
-No. Seriously, I just thought of it.
-Since I'm close with Ga-yeon…

1122
00:51:50,440 --> 00:51:52,442
-Since I'm close with Ga-yeon,
-No.

1123
00:51:52,526 --> 00:51:55,487
-you came to hear that answer.
-No.

1124
00:51:55,570 --> 00:51:57,781
He wanted to ask me about Ga-yeon.

1125
00:51:57,864 --> 00:51:59,658
It's so funny when I'm with him.

1126
00:51:59,741 --> 00:52:02,160
-I had fun, buddy.
-Yeah. Bye.

1127
00:52:02,244 --> 00:52:04,204
HYE-WON AND JUNG-MIN
SECRET DATE ENDS

1128
00:52:04,704 --> 00:52:07,958
CAFE HAUS HAIL
SECRET DATE

1129
00:52:28,144 --> 00:52:29,187
Hey, Ga-yeon.

1130
00:52:29,813 --> 00:52:32,607
GA-YEON AND JUNG-MIN
SECRET DATE

1131
00:52:32,691 --> 00:52:34,651
It's a secret date, finally.

1132
00:52:35,277 --> 00:52:37,362
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

1133
00:52:37,445 --> 00:52:39,197
You got here early.

1134
00:52:39,281 --> 00:52:40,782
About five minutes early?

1135
00:52:40,866 --> 00:52:41,867
I'm not sure.

1136
00:52:41,950 --> 00:52:44,035
SLURP

1137
00:52:46,204 --> 00:52:47,914
We should've gone out yesterday.

1138
00:52:50,125 --> 00:52:55,046
I went on a date with Kyung-ho
and had a long chat with him.

1139
00:52:55,130 --> 00:52:57,048
So I got an idea about

1140
00:52:57,132 --> 00:52:59,968
what kind of person he is
and what he's like in a relationship.

1141
00:53:00,051 --> 00:53:03,597
But I have no idea about Jung-min.

1142
00:53:03,680 --> 00:53:08,810
I'm going to try my best to figure out
what kind of person he is.

1143
00:53:08,894 --> 00:53:13,273
I'm sure I'll have some kind of feeling
during that conversation, right?

1144
00:53:13,356 --> 00:53:17,068
I think I'll see what that feeling is
and make my final decision.

1145
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:19,988
-We've only talked back at the house.
-Yeah.

1146
00:53:20,071 --> 00:53:21,531
We never got to do it outside.

1147
00:53:22,032 --> 00:53:24,951
We never got to have a deep conversation.

1148
00:53:26,202 --> 00:53:28,371
I feel more nervous for some reason

1149
00:53:28,455 --> 00:53:30,290
-than in front of the fireplace.
-Right?

1150
00:53:30,373 --> 00:53:32,876
I feel awkward for some reason.

1151
00:53:32,959 --> 00:53:33,919
Yeah.

1152
00:53:36,254 --> 00:53:37,213
Until now,

1153
00:53:37,964 --> 00:53:39,799
I've dated people

1154
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:43,178
that I have been attracted to.

1155
00:53:43,803 --> 00:53:45,555
-Yeah, I'd go for someone…
-That's good.

1156
00:53:45,639 --> 00:53:46,806
…I have good feelings about.

1157
00:53:47,432 --> 00:53:49,476
That's the kind of relationships I had.

1158
00:53:49,559 --> 00:53:52,228
When I was in relationships like that,

1159
00:53:52,312 --> 00:53:53,688
I've gotten hurt.

1160
00:53:53,772 --> 00:53:57,108
So the man I'd like to date in the future

1161
00:53:57,192 --> 00:53:59,736
should be older and settled in life.

1162
00:54:00,695 --> 00:54:02,948
Someone who is relaxed
in the way they speak and act?

1163
00:54:03,031 --> 00:54:07,243
I want to be in a relationship
where the guy can keep me grounded.

1164
00:54:07,327 --> 00:54:08,912
That was my mindset when I came here.

1165
00:54:10,246 --> 00:54:11,164
But

1166
00:54:11,247 --> 00:54:15,335
when you chose me as the person
you wanted to go on a date with,

1167
00:54:15,919 --> 00:54:16,878
we held hands, right?

1168
00:54:16,962 --> 00:54:18,922
-We talked while we held hands.
-Yeah.

1169
00:54:19,506 --> 00:54:22,634
Would you go on a date with me tomorrow?

1170
00:54:22,717 --> 00:54:23,551
I'd love that.

1171
00:54:25,095 --> 00:54:27,222
<i>That was huge for me.</i>

1172
00:54:27,305 --> 00:54:29,349
I wasn't interested in you at first,

1173
00:54:29,432 --> 00:54:31,935
but I opened up to you after that.

1174
00:54:32,018 --> 00:54:36,481
That's why I started having
romantic feelings for you.

1175
00:54:37,107 --> 00:54:39,192
But my eyes would

1176
00:54:39,275 --> 00:54:43,697
drift to where Kyung-ho is sometimes.

1177
00:54:43,780 --> 00:54:46,449
I didn't know why though.

1178
00:54:46,533 --> 00:54:49,661
I wanted to check my feelings for him.

1179
00:54:49,744 --> 00:54:55,959
Then,
I realized that I had romantic feelings

1180
00:54:56,042 --> 00:54:57,752
for him too.

1181
00:54:57,836 --> 00:54:59,587
But those feelings

1182
00:54:59,671 --> 00:55:03,341
were smaller than
the romantic feelings I had for you.

1183
00:55:03,425 --> 00:55:04,634
A lot smaller.

1184
00:55:04,718 --> 00:55:10,807
Anyway, I've been thinking about it
since last night until this morning.

1185
00:55:10,890 --> 00:55:13,560
But I still don't know.

1186
00:55:14,144 --> 00:55:16,855
I don't know how I feel exactly.

1187
00:55:16,938 --> 00:55:20,525
The person I want to date
and the person I'm attracted to.

1188
00:55:20,608 --> 00:55:23,862
The two are so different.

1189
00:55:25,488 --> 00:55:28,491
<i>I realized that Ga-yeon was conflicted.</i>

1190
00:55:28,575 --> 00:55:29,743
I didn't show it,

1191
00:55:29,826 --> 00:55:32,912
but my heart sank.

1192
00:55:32,996 --> 00:55:35,457
<i>I was a little unnerved by it.</i>

1193
00:55:35,540 --> 00:55:38,334
I thought we got along well
when we hung out.

1194
00:55:38,418 --> 00:55:41,588
It was just fun
without thinking about anything.

1195
00:55:41,671 --> 00:55:43,798
<i>When we took selfies together,</i>

1196
00:55:43,882 --> 00:55:45,842
<i>it was just naturally fun.</i>

1197
00:55:46,342 --> 00:55:48,845
My interest in you grew a lot.

1198
00:55:48,928 --> 00:55:50,555
That's why I put a lot of Heart Chips
in yours.

1199
00:55:51,556 --> 00:55:54,142
I think I'll use up my Heart Chips
and choose you.

1200
00:55:55,393 --> 00:55:56,728
But

1201
00:55:56,811 --> 00:55:59,689
this is our first date, isn't it?
And we have to decide tomorrow.

1202
00:56:00,774 --> 00:56:02,108
I'm a bit sad about that.

1203
00:56:02,192 --> 00:56:03,443
You expressed

1204
00:56:04,235 --> 00:56:08,198
how you felt about me publicly.

1205
00:56:08,281 --> 00:56:10,700
And I responded to that too.

1206
00:56:10,784 --> 00:56:12,744
-Acting lovey-dovey?
-Yeah.

1207
00:56:13,453 --> 00:56:14,996
I like it and it gets me excited.

1208
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:16,247
-Really?
-Yeah.

1209
00:56:16,331 --> 00:56:17,415
Of course.

1210
00:56:17,499 --> 00:56:21,586
Even your actions and light touches

1211
00:56:21,669 --> 00:56:23,588
have comforted me a lot.

1212
00:56:23,671 --> 00:56:25,173
I am thankful but…

1213
00:56:25,256 --> 00:56:26,382
"Thanks."

1214
00:56:26,466 --> 00:56:27,884
"Heart Chips for Do-geon."

1215
00:56:28,927 --> 00:56:30,345
"Thanks. Now, Kyung-ho."

1216
00:56:30,428 --> 00:56:31,262
"Thanks!"

1217
00:56:31,346 --> 00:56:33,973
No, it wasn't like that.

1218
00:56:34,057 --> 00:56:34,891
"Thanks."

1219
00:56:34,974 --> 00:56:36,476
"This is hard. Who should I choose?"

1220
00:56:37,143 --> 00:56:38,728
Wait. Time out.

1221
00:56:38,812 --> 00:56:40,230
-Time out?
-Time out.

1222
00:56:40,313 --> 00:56:44,692
I started having feelings for you
when we held hands.

1223
00:56:44,776 --> 00:56:47,487
That was very big for me. Tremendously.

1224
00:56:47,570 --> 00:56:49,239
What if that wasn't me?

1225
00:56:53,993 --> 00:56:55,370
What if that was Kyung-ho?

1226
00:56:57,997 --> 00:57:00,625
I don't have to think about it.
It didn't happen.

1227
00:57:00,708 --> 00:57:01,876
Really?

1228
00:57:01,960 --> 00:57:04,295
Gosh, this won't do.

1229
00:57:04,379 --> 00:57:06,214
I have to stay right by your side today.

1230
00:57:06,297 --> 00:57:07,423
"Hey, Kyung-ho."

1231
00:57:07,507 --> 00:57:09,467
"Shouldn't you sit over there?"

1232
00:57:10,468 --> 00:57:12,637
Can I be selfish like that?

1233
00:57:14,848 --> 00:57:16,975
I won't give him a chance to get close.

1234
00:57:17,058 --> 00:57:19,269
-What do you think about my strategy?
-It'll be funny.

1235
00:57:19,352 --> 00:57:21,771
I wanted to hold hands with you
if we went on a date.

1236
00:57:22,522 --> 00:57:23,731
Can we hold hands?

1237
00:57:26,359 --> 00:57:27,318
Hey.

1238
00:57:28,903 --> 00:57:31,239
Are you doing that
because I said this meant a lot?

1239
00:57:31,322 --> 00:57:34,200
No, I really was going to
hold your hand as soon as it started.

1240
00:57:34,784 --> 00:57:35,869
Give me your hand.

1241
00:57:36,911 --> 00:57:38,455
-No.
-Let me help you out.

1242
00:57:38,538 --> 00:57:39,456
Give it.

1243
00:57:39,539 --> 00:57:41,666
-Let me give you a good tip.
-What?

1244
00:57:41,749 --> 00:57:43,418
-It's the last time.
-Just one.

1245
00:57:44,043 --> 00:57:44,919
Look.

1246
00:57:45,920 --> 00:57:49,174
Hold hands like this.

1247
00:57:49,257 --> 00:57:50,717
Hold hands with me…

1248
00:57:50,800 --> 00:57:52,385
-And Kyung-ho?
-…and with Kyung-ho too.

1249
00:57:52,469 --> 00:57:54,179
-You're insane.
-You'll realize that

1250
00:57:54,846 --> 00:57:56,514
you don't feel anything with him.

1251
00:57:56,598 --> 00:57:58,892
Maybe you'll think that way.

1252
00:57:58,975 --> 00:58:01,227
-You want me to hold hands with Kyung-ho?
-Yeah.

1253
00:58:01,311 --> 00:58:02,645
Hold hands with him.

1254
00:58:04,272 --> 00:58:05,690
You'll feel it for yourself.

1255
00:58:05,773 --> 00:58:08,443
Real nice tip. Real nice.

1256
00:58:08,526 --> 00:58:10,528
-I'll get going.
-It ended.

1257
00:58:10,612 --> 00:58:11,613
I know.

1258
00:58:11,696 --> 00:58:13,156
See you back at the house.

1259
00:58:15,033 --> 00:58:17,327
-Shaking hands? Let's lace our fingers.
-No.

1260
00:58:18,119 --> 00:58:19,621
-Okay. See you later.
-Okay.

1261
00:58:19,704 --> 00:58:20,872
Is this Kyung-ho's seat?

1262
00:58:20,955 --> 00:58:22,248
No.

1263
00:58:22,332 --> 00:58:24,125
I ought to break this.

1264
00:58:28,254 --> 00:58:30,256
-Bye.
-I want to bolt this chair down.

1265
00:58:30,965 --> 00:58:32,342
-Bye.
-Bye.

1266
00:58:32,425 --> 00:58:33,843
GA-YEON AND JUNG-MIN
SECRET DATE ENDS

1267
00:58:33,927 --> 00:58:35,970
I was jealous,

1268
00:58:36,054 --> 00:58:38,640
but I didn't think
she would change her mind.

1269
00:58:38,723 --> 00:58:43,645
I didn't expect to be so conflicted,

1270
00:58:43,728 --> 00:58:49,609
so I did feel bad that Kyung-ho jumped in.

1271
00:58:50,193 --> 00:58:51,653
She's the same age as me, right?

1272
00:58:51,736 --> 00:58:53,655
She's starting to think about marriage.

1273
00:58:53,738 --> 00:58:56,824
-Jung-min would make such a good spouse.
-Totally.

1274
00:58:56,908 --> 00:58:58,243
-I think so too.
-Yeah.

1275
00:58:58,326 --> 00:58:59,327
That's why she's conflicted.

1276
00:58:59,410 --> 00:59:01,412
She's talking about
attraction and whatnot.

1277
00:59:01,496 --> 00:59:03,665
-But it's about marriage material.
-Reality.

1278
00:59:03,748 --> 00:59:05,083
-Yeah, the reality.
-Right.

1279
00:59:06,125 --> 00:59:08,461
GA-YEON IS WAITING FOR ANOTHER

1280
00:59:21,975 --> 00:59:26,604
GA-YEON AND KYUNG-HO
SECRET DATE

1281
00:59:30,984 --> 00:59:33,111
What did you talk about yesterday?

1282
00:59:34,070 --> 00:59:36,781
You and Ye-rim looked

1283
00:59:36,864 --> 00:59:38,533
very upset yesterday.

1284
00:59:38,616 --> 00:59:41,035
Yesterday? We didn't talk about much.

1285
00:59:41,119 --> 00:59:42,829
-Are you curious?
-Yeah.

1286
00:59:42,912 --> 00:59:44,330
After our date yesterday,

1287
00:59:45,790 --> 00:59:48,501
my mind was somewhat made up,

1288
00:59:48,585 --> 00:59:50,128
so I just told Ye-rim that.

1289
00:59:50,712 --> 00:59:52,213
I said I like you more.

1290
00:59:55,258 --> 00:59:56,843
Why? Is it funny?

1291
00:59:57,427 --> 00:59:58,261
It isn't funny.

1292
00:59:58,344 --> 00:59:59,470
Why did you laugh?

1293
01:00:00,513 --> 01:00:01,472
Anyway…

1294
01:00:01,556 --> 01:00:03,308
Both of you looked upset.

1295
01:00:03,391 --> 01:00:06,436
-Yeah, we couldn't be in a good mood.
-Right.

1296
01:00:06,519 --> 01:00:08,187
So that's how you feel?

1297
01:00:10,315 --> 01:00:13,359
I'm only going to express interest in you.

1298
01:00:15,903 --> 01:00:17,655
That's that.

1299
01:00:20,867 --> 01:00:22,327
Where do you want me to start?

1300
01:00:22,410 --> 01:00:24,078
Just tell me what you want to tell me.

1301
01:00:24,162 --> 01:00:25,622
-You decide.
-You tell me.

1302
01:00:25,705 --> 01:00:28,458
-Okay?
-Do you want me to start from one?

1303
01:00:28,541 --> 01:00:29,876
From one to eight.

1304
01:00:29,959 --> 01:00:31,419
But eight is most important.

1305
01:00:31,502 --> 01:00:32,879
I don't want to know everything.

1306
01:00:32,962 --> 01:00:34,422
The latter part is more important.

1307
01:00:34,505 --> 01:00:37,342
Then, give me from eight to ten.

1308
01:00:37,425 --> 01:00:39,594
No, how about seven to nine?

1309
01:00:40,386 --> 01:00:42,847
When we chose our dates,

1310
01:00:42,930 --> 01:00:46,893
I told you that Jung-min holding my hand
played a huge part.

1311
01:00:47,852 --> 01:00:51,648
SHE ENDED UP STARTED FROM 1

1312
01:00:52,899 --> 01:00:55,234
AND ARRIVED NEAR 7

1313
01:00:55,318 --> 01:00:58,154
To be honest, our date made me

1314
01:00:58,237 --> 01:01:00,657
feel very comfortable.

1315
01:01:00,740 --> 01:01:01,908
Yeah.

1316
01:01:01,991 --> 01:01:05,495
All the constellations show up like this…

1317
01:01:05,578 --> 01:01:08,456
<i>The conversation we had in the car</i>

1318
01:01:10,124 --> 01:01:13,002
<i>and the looks we exchanged</i>

1319
01:01:14,337 --> 01:01:15,713
kept coming to mind

1320
01:01:17,048 --> 01:01:18,341
even after we got back.

1321
01:01:18,424 --> 01:01:22,345
Even then, I was still in denial
about my feelings for you.

1322
01:01:22,929 --> 01:01:25,306
I wanted to deny it.

1323
01:01:25,390 --> 01:01:26,641
-I see.
-Yeah.

1324
01:01:26,724 --> 01:01:29,268
But somehow…

1325
01:01:29,352 --> 01:01:30,353
That's it.

1326
01:01:36,025 --> 01:01:37,777
-So you want to talk?
-I can't make up my mind.

1327
01:01:37,860 --> 01:01:39,696
-You can't make up your mind?
-No.

1328
01:01:39,779 --> 01:01:44,742
You were in the living room feeling upset.

1329
01:01:44,826 --> 01:01:47,120
I was really sleepy that day,

1330
01:01:47,203 --> 01:01:49,580
but I didn't want to go in the room
because you were there.

1331
01:01:50,164 --> 01:01:52,208
AFTER YE-RIM AND KYUNG-HO
TALKED LAST NIGHT

1332
01:01:52,291 --> 01:01:53,793
Why are you doing the dishes now?

1333
01:01:53,876 --> 01:01:55,420
I ate out of these.

1334
01:01:55,503 --> 01:01:57,255
GA-YEON DREW KYUNG-HO

1335
01:01:57,338 --> 01:01:58,297
Didn't I do a good job?

1336
01:01:59,173 --> 01:02:00,216
-Didn't I do well?
-You did.

1337
01:02:00,299 --> 01:02:01,676
-Good drawing.
-Right?

1338
01:02:02,301 --> 01:02:04,971
When you're there, I want to be near you.

1339
01:02:05,722 --> 01:02:07,056
Because I felt that way…

1340
01:02:07,140 --> 01:02:08,516
This morning,

1341
01:02:08,599 --> 01:02:11,185
<i>you were drawing at the table</i>

1342
01:02:11,269 --> 01:02:13,521
<i>and Jung-min was lying on the sofa.</i>

1343
01:02:14,313 --> 01:02:17,233
<i>But I went over to your side.</i>

1344
01:02:19,402 --> 01:02:20,695
Draw an angel too.

1345
01:02:21,237 --> 01:02:25,491
I kept feeling like
my body and eyes are drawn to you.

1346
01:02:25,575 --> 01:02:29,579
But I don't know what this is.

1347
01:02:30,204 --> 01:02:31,706
It's annoying

1348
01:02:31,789 --> 01:02:33,541
and I'm confused.

1349
01:02:33,624 --> 01:02:35,752
That's how I feel right now.

1350
01:02:35,835 --> 01:02:37,962
-You're not sorted out yet?
-No.

1351
01:02:38,713 --> 01:02:42,842
If I got a chance to go on a date today,
I wanted to go with Jung-min

1352
01:02:42,925 --> 01:02:45,511
because we never got to go on a date.

1353
01:02:45,595 --> 01:02:48,347
That's why I wanted to make him king.

1354
01:02:48,431 --> 01:02:50,933
I put a lot in yours to make you king.

1355
01:02:51,017 --> 01:02:52,727
Why would you make me king?

1356
01:02:52,810 --> 01:02:54,395
I wanted you to choose for yourself.

1357
01:02:54,479 --> 01:02:56,314
I didn't want that.

1358
01:02:56,397 --> 01:02:58,149
But I wanted it.

1359
01:02:58,232 --> 01:03:00,568
What if I chose Jung-min

1360
01:03:00,651 --> 01:03:02,361
-for the date?
-I thought you would.

1361
01:03:02,445 --> 01:03:03,613
Even so?

1362
01:03:03,696 --> 01:03:04,697
Yeah.

1363
01:03:04,781 --> 01:03:07,408
Then, it would make

1364
01:03:07,492 --> 01:03:10,787
Jung-min and me more official.

1365
01:03:10,870 --> 01:03:12,705
I wouldn't think that.

1366
01:03:13,748 --> 01:03:15,750
I'm only going to think
in a way that benefits me.

1367
01:03:16,501 --> 01:03:19,337
It's true that you haven't
gone on a date with Jung-min.

1368
01:03:19,420 --> 01:03:22,548
You should've already gone
on a date, but you couldn't.

1369
01:03:22,632 --> 01:03:25,927
I still don't know what's right even now.

1370
01:03:26,010 --> 01:03:27,345
If I were you,

1371
01:03:29,138 --> 01:03:30,264
I'd go with the one I'm drawn to.

1372
01:03:31,015 --> 01:03:32,099
If I were you.

1373
01:03:32,183 --> 01:03:34,393
I'm not just saying that for my sake.

1374
01:03:34,477 --> 01:03:35,978
I really would have done that.

1375
01:03:37,355 --> 01:03:41,192
It isn't that I wasn't attracted
to Jung-min at all.

1376
01:03:41,275 --> 01:03:42,443
Of course not.

1377
01:03:42,527 --> 01:03:44,237
He is kind, considerate,

1378
01:03:44,320 --> 01:03:48,115
and he showed subtle physical affection

1379
01:03:48,199 --> 01:03:50,785
with or without drawing attention.

1380
01:03:50,868 --> 01:03:54,539
I didn't reject all of that.
I let him do it

1381
01:03:54,622 --> 01:03:57,208
and it made my heart flutter,
to be honest.

1382
01:03:57,291 --> 01:03:59,126
You like physical affection, don't you?

1383
01:03:59,710 --> 01:04:00,962
-No.
-Okay.

1384
01:04:01,045 --> 01:04:02,171
-Wait.
-What?

1385
01:04:02,255 --> 01:04:04,131
What's wrong with light touches?

1386
01:04:04,215 --> 01:04:05,091
Yeah.

1387
01:04:06,759 --> 01:04:07,969
It was huge for me…

1388
01:04:08,052 --> 01:04:10,179
-I'm sure.
-…when we first held hands.

1389
01:04:10,263 --> 01:04:13,224
Since I'm confused, Jung-min gave me

1390
01:04:13,307 --> 01:04:15,476
a solution before he left.

1391
01:04:15,560 --> 01:04:16,602
What did he say?

1392
01:04:16,686 --> 01:04:18,479
He said I should hold his hand.

1393
01:04:18,563 --> 01:04:20,314
-And…
-I don't want to hear it.

1394
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:22,441
Go ahead.

1395
01:04:22,525 --> 01:04:24,610
He said I should hold your hand too.

1396
01:04:24,694 --> 01:04:25,736
Then,

1397
01:04:26,654 --> 01:04:27,989
he said I'll know.

1398
01:04:28,072 --> 01:04:30,074
So I said I won't do it.

1399
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:31,993
You don't want to hold my hand?

1400
01:04:32,076 --> 01:04:33,953
-That's not what I mean.
-Okay.

1401
01:04:34,036 --> 01:04:35,496
Can you give me your phone for a second?

1402
01:04:35,580 --> 01:04:36,956
My phone?

1403
01:04:37,039 --> 01:04:38,708
-I'm going to write it down.
-Okay.

1404
01:04:39,417 --> 01:04:41,419
I really can't say it out loud.

1405
01:04:42,169 --> 01:04:44,046
-Read it when I'm not around.
-Okay.

1406
01:04:44,630 --> 01:04:47,633
This is what I want to tell you now,

1407
01:04:47,717 --> 01:04:49,844
but it's really what I wanted to tell you

1408
01:04:51,095 --> 01:04:53,097
yesterday. Anyway…

1409
01:04:53,180 --> 01:04:54,223
Should I rewrite it?

1410
01:05:08,654 --> 01:05:10,114
-I'll read it in the car.
-Okay.

1411
01:05:11,532 --> 01:05:12,450
Should I delete it?

1412
01:05:14,994 --> 01:05:19,081
The way I act when I talk to you
is so different from

1413
01:05:19,165 --> 01:05:21,584
the way I act
when I interact with Jung-min.

1414
01:05:21,667 --> 01:05:22,501
I'm curious.

1415
01:05:22,585 --> 01:05:24,587
It's so different.
If I talk with Jung-min--

1416
01:05:24,670 --> 01:05:26,213
Why do you show us different sides?

1417
01:05:26,297 --> 01:05:28,049
I become more of an adult.

1418
01:05:28,132 --> 01:05:31,928
When I'm talking with Jung-min,
I talk more maturely.

1419
01:05:32,011 --> 01:05:33,804
-Really?
-Yeah.

1420
01:05:33,888 --> 01:05:35,598
It must be because I'm younger.

1421
01:05:35,681 --> 01:05:36,974
Because I'm young.

1422
01:05:37,058 --> 01:05:38,142
Yeah.

1423
01:05:41,145 --> 01:05:43,022
<i>He flirts in a cute way.</i>

1424
01:05:43,105 --> 01:05:46,150
<i>He flirts like a younger guy.</i>

1425
01:05:46,233 --> 01:05:49,695
When I'm with Kyung-ho, I can be at ease

1426
01:05:49,779 --> 01:05:52,573
while laughing with him.

1427
01:05:52,657 --> 01:05:54,909
Then, my heart would skip a beat
out of nowhere.

1428
01:05:55,785 --> 01:05:56,911
It must be over.

1429
01:05:57,703 --> 01:06:00,247
THE SECRET DATE HAS ENDED

1430
01:06:00,831 --> 01:06:02,667
You're going to make your mind up, right?

1431
01:06:05,711 --> 01:06:08,047
It's hard. It's so hard.

1432
01:06:08,130 --> 01:06:10,257
-You'll do well. You're an adult.
-I'm sure I will.

1433
01:06:11,509 --> 01:06:12,927
-Bye.
-Okay.

1434
01:06:13,427 --> 01:06:17,723
She may have more feelings for Jung-min.

1435
01:06:17,807 --> 01:06:20,351
<i>I don't know if she could tell or not,</i>

1436
01:06:20,434 --> 01:06:22,019
<i>but I was nervous.</i>

1437
01:06:22,103 --> 01:06:27,942
I didn't feel like
she was leaning toward me.

1438
01:06:28,025 --> 01:06:32,071
When I spoke to two different men
in the same place and same spot,

1439
01:06:32,154 --> 01:06:34,115
I realized once again that

1440
01:06:34,198 --> 01:06:37,910
I act one way with one person
but another way with the other.

1441
01:06:37,994 --> 01:06:41,330
When I'm with Jung-min, I become calmer.

1442
01:06:41,414 --> 01:06:43,499
It's more fun and my heart flutters too.

1443
01:06:43,582 --> 01:06:45,751
But when I am with Kyung-ho,

1444
01:06:45,835 --> 01:06:48,921
I feel a bit tense

1445
01:06:49,005 --> 01:06:53,634
and I'm left with
lingering feelings afterward.

1446
01:06:53,718 --> 01:06:57,555
SHE CHECKS KYUNG-HO'S MESSAGE
AFTER THE DATE

1447
01:06:59,181 --> 01:07:01,767
I HOPE YOU CAN ORGANIZE YOUR THOUGHTS
AROUND WHAT'S BEST FOR YOU

1448
01:07:01,851 --> 01:07:05,771
<i>He made a signature for me.</i>

1449
01:07:06,856 --> 01:07:08,858
I wanted to give her a boost.

1450
01:07:08,941 --> 01:07:10,026
I hoped she would

1451
01:07:11,193 --> 01:07:12,570
become stronger.

1452
01:07:12,653 --> 01:07:14,530
I also hoped she was touched by me.

1453
01:07:20,286 --> 01:07:24,081
SECRET DATE
CAFE BONJOUR

1454
01:07:27,168 --> 01:07:28,044
Hi.

1455
01:07:28,627 --> 01:07:29,628
Hello.

1456
01:07:31,547 --> 01:07:33,924
<i>I thought the moment had finally arrived.</i>

1457
01:07:34,008 --> 01:07:37,762
"What if I requested him
but he didn't want to talk to me?"

1458
01:07:37,845 --> 01:07:39,680
I was worried about that.

1459
01:07:43,267 --> 01:07:44,226
Use the blanket.

1460
01:07:45,519 --> 01:07:47,855
Did you know I'd ask for you?

1461
01:07:48,647 --> 01:07:49,774
You requested me?

1462
01:07:49,857 --> 01:07:51,067
Did you request me?

1463
01:07:51,609 --> 01:07:52,651
I requested you.

1464
01:07:52,735 --> 01:07:53,903
-Really?
-Yeah.

1465
01:07:53,986 --> 01:07:55,112
-I requested you too.
-Yeah?

1466
01:07:55,196 --> 01:07:56,238
YE-RIM AND KYUNG-HO
SECRET DATE

1467
01:07:56,322 --> 01:07:57,948
I regretted what I said when I woke up.

1468
01:07:58,032 --> 01:07:58,866
Why?

1469
01:07:58,949 --> 01:08:01,202
I think I was argumentative last night.

1470
01:08:03,329 --> 01:08:05,289
No, you weren't argumentative.

1471
01:08:05,956 --> 01:08:06,957
I was just scolded.

1472
01:08:11,754 --> 01:08:14,340
You didn't avoid me today?

1473
01:08:14,423 --> 01:08:15,257
-You?
-Yeah.

1474
01:08:15,341 --> 01:08:17,384
-No, I tried not to avoid you.
-Really?

1475
01:08:17,468 --> 01:08:20,554
But it felt like you were scared of me.

1476
01:08:20,638 --> 01:08:22,264
Of course I'm scared of you.

1477
01:08:22,348 --> 01:08:25,142
-I'm scared.
-I got scared of you being scared

1478
01:08:26,102 --> 01:08:27,603
since you won't speak to me.

1479
01:08:27,686 --> 01:08:28,729
I mean…

1480
01:08:28,813 --> 01:08:30,689
I tried to stay within your vicinity

1481
01:08:30,773 --> 01:08:33,067
and join the conversation.

1482
01:08:33,150 --> 01:08:34,527
Yeah, you did.

1483
01:08:35,069 --> 01:08:36,987
THIS MORNING

1484
01:08:37,071 --> 01:08:38,823
HOVERING AROUND

1485
01:08:41,742 --> 01:08:42,993
What's on your mind?

1486
01:08:43,077 --> 01:08:44,829
SUDDEN COUNSELING SESSION

1487
01:08:44,912 --> 01:08:46,705
I reached out to reconcile last night.

1488
01:08:46,789 --> 01:08:47,915
You did.

1489
01:08:49,041 --> 01:08:50,626
I admire your courage.

1490
01:08:51,127 --> 01:08:52,711
Let's be friends.

1491
01:08:55,005 --> 01:08:56,382
Okay.

1492
01:08:56,465 --> 01:08:57,591
Thanks.

1493
01:08:57,675 --> 01:09:00,344
Do you still feel the same way?

1494
01:09:02,263 --> 01:09:03,472
-Feel the same way?
-Yeah.

1495
01:09:05,724 --> 01:09:06,809
I…

1496
01:09:09,311 --> 01:09:12,398
I choose Ga-yeon.

1497
01:09:16,610 --> 01:09:17,611
That's how I feel.

1498
01:09:17,695 --> 01:09:18,612
Why?

1499
01:09:28,622 --> 01:09:30,374
To be honest,

1500
01:09:30,457 --> 01:09:32,084
I don't know if I should

1501
01:09:32,668 --> 01:09:34,003
tell you this or not.

1502
01:09:34,086 --> 01:09:36,714
-Anyway, I should be honest with you.
-Okay.

1503
01:09:36,797 --> 01:09:38,674
I have a younger sister.

1504
01:09:39,300 --> 01:09:40,301
She's the same age as you.

1505
01:09:42,720 --> 01:09:43,929
Since a long time ago,

1506
01:09:44,013 --> 01:09:46,932
when someone is the same age as my sister,

1507
01:09:47,850 --> 01:09:51,687
I don't view them as a woman.
I even said that during the pre-meeting.

1508
01:09:52,855 --> 01:09:54,481
One sister is five years older than me

1509
01:09:54,565 --> 01:09:56,525
and my other sister is
four years younger than me.

1510
01:09:56,609 --> 01:10:00,905
But whether it's three, two, one,
five, or six years, it doesn't matter.

1511
01:10:00,988 --> 01:10:03,490
Strangely though,
it's weird if they're the same age.

1512
01:10:03,574 --> 01:10:05,910
The moment I find out
they're four years younger than me,

1513
01:10:07,453 --> 01:10:09,496
it makes me feel distant.

1514
01:10:09,580 --> 01:10:11,665
I didn't know
if I should say that to you--

1515
01:10:11,749 --> 01:10:14,627
I'm so thankful that you told me that.

1516
01:10:14,710 --> 01:10:18,464
You kept saying that age didn't matter.

1517
01:10:18,964 --> 01:10:21,675
But I could sense
the immediate distance between us.

1518
01:10:21,759 --> 01:10:23,344
22 years old?

1519
01:10:23,928 --> 01:10:25,179
We're done for.

1520
01:10:25,262 --> 01:10:26,764
What did I do when I was 22?

1521
01:10:26,847 --> 01:10:29,141
Are you trying to put distance between us?

1522
01:10:29,225 --> 01:10:33,020
But the number two and two
is a bit shocking.

1523
01:10:35,147 --> 01:10:37,942
<i>So that was why I felt</i>
<i>the distance between us.</i>

1524
01:10:38,651 --> 01:10:42,446
I felt like he was
no longer curious about me.

1525
01:10:42,529 --> 01:10:43,656
If you were…

1526
01:10:44,615 --> 01:10:48,369
Honestly, if you were a different age,

1527
01:10:48,452 --> 01:10:50,829
I really do think things
would have been different.

1528
01:10:52,122 --> 01:10:53,457
Get mad at him, Joo-heon.

1529
01:10:54,041 --> 01:10:56,210
Anyway, from Kyung-ho's perspective,

1530
01:10:56,293 --> 01:10:57,878
the age must have been

1531
01:10:57,962 --> 01:10:59,630
a really important issue.

1532
01:10:59,713 --> 01:11:01,048
Even if it was important,

1533
01:11:01,131 --> 01:11:03,384
he shouldn't have said,
"Things might have been different."

1534
01:11:03,467 --> 01:11:04,927
Yeah, he shouldn't have said that.

1535
01:11:05,010 --> 01:11:06,971
It would've been better not to say… Hey!

1536
01:11:08,180 --> 01:11:10,641
I really do think things
would have been different.

1537
01:11:10,724 --> 01:11:12,309
I did think that too.

1538
01:11:12,393 --> 01:11:15,521
If I were two years older than you,

1539
01:11:15,604 --> 01:11:19,233
you would have liked me
even if I didn't make any effort.

1540
01:11:20,693 --> 01:11:22,111
From that aspect,

1541
01:11:22,736 --> 01:11:24,029
I'm jealous of Ga-yeon

1542
01:11:25,447 --> 01:11:27,032
and I wish I was…

1543
01:11:31,120 --> 01:11:32,496
You're right.

1544
01:11:32,579 --> 01:11:35,332
It shouldn't be a big deal.
Age is just a number.

1545
01:11:35,416 --> 01:11:37,918
-But not 22 years old.
-Right.

1546
01:11:38,919 --> 01:11:40,379
Just not that.

1547
01:11:41,672 --> 01:11:43,257
What did you want to

1548
01:11:44,425 --> 01:11:46,468
-talk about?
-Our conversation?

1549
01:11:47,803 --> 01:11:52,558
I don't think I even know
what kind of person you are.

1550
01:11:52,641 --> 01:11:55,185
And I wanted you to know
what kind of person I was too.

1551
01:11:56,103 --> 01:11:57,354
What kind of person are you?

1552
01:11:58,355 --> 01:12:00,983
First of all, I don't like playing games.

1553
01:12:01,692 --> 01:12:03,902
Either I like someone or I don't.

1554
01:12:06,655 --> 01:12:07,573
Actually,

1555
01:12:09,116 --> 01:12:12,578
I did think you would change your mind
if I did my best.

1556
01:12:15,664 --> 01:12:18,292
That's why I don't think it's over yet.

1557
01:12:20,002 --> 01:12:21,503
Right, it isn't over yet.

1558
01:12:24,715 --> 01:12:26,008
Anyway.

1559
01:12:27,009 --> 01:12:29,678
Also, I was worried that I was

1560
01:12:29,762 --> 01:12:31,930
making you feel uncomfortable.

1561
01:12:32,014 --> 01:12:33,766
I didn't want you to feel pressured.

1562
01:12:35,059 --> 01:12:39,730
From the moment you said
you were curious about someone else,

1563
01:12:40,397 --> 01:12:43,859
I didn't want to make it
uncomfortable for you.

1564
01:12:43,942 --> 01:12:46,945
Of course, I want the person I like
to feel at ease.

1565
01:12:47,029 --> 01:12:48,655
I really appreciate that.

1566
01:12:48,739 --> 01:12:51,992
That's why I waited until

1567
01:12:52,785 --> 01:12:53,994
