1568
01:12:54,078 --> 01:12:55,996
You're happy when you meet outside.

1569
01:12:56,080 --> 01:12:57,998
Do your feelings grow more than in here?

1570
01:12:58,082 --> 01:12:59,708
Only Kyung-ho grilled the meat.

1571
01:12:59,792 --> 01:13:01,585
What? I helped out too.

1572
01:13:04,671 --> 01:13:05,798
I did that,

1573
01:13:07,049 --> 01:13:08,926
but I didn't know
it would turn out like this.

1574
01:13:09,968 --> 01:13:11,053
But it isn't over yet.

1575
01:13:11,136 --> 01:13:13,013
I know. I'm not that young.

1576
01:13:13,722 --> 01:13:15,432
Yeah, I know.

1577
01:13:15,516 --> 01:13:18,727
<i>I really tried my best to explain.</i>

1578
01:13:18,811 --> 01:13:21,563
<i>Even though he said</i>
<i>he's sure about his feelings for Ga-yeon,</i>

1579
01:13:21,647 --> 01:13:24,233
we didn't get to have a real chat.

1580
01:13:24,316 --> 01:13:25,401
No regrets?

1581
01:13:25,484 --> 01:13:28,946
I'm going to keep knocking like that.

1582
01:13:29,029 --> 01:13:31,865
I went into that conversation
with the intention of being

1583
01:13:31,949 --> 01:13:35,452
honest and talking about everything
so that I'd have no regrets.

1584
01:13:35,536 --> 01:13:36,620
Good job.

1585
01:13:37,246 --> 01:13:38,872
-Either way…
-It's better than just pouting.

1586
01:13:38,956 --> 01:13:40,249
She found her direction.

1587
01:13:40,332 --> 01:13:43,419
As I told you in the beginning,

1588
01:13:43,502 --> 01:13:46,630
you really have the face that I am into.

1589
01:13:47,673 --> 01:13:48,715
It's embarrassing.

1590
01:13:50,050 --> 01:13:52,010
And you actually

1591
01:13:52,594 --> 01:13:54,555
have the personality that I like.

1592
01:13:54,638 --> 01:13:57,599
I think there's something cool
about people who speak with ease

1593
01:13:58,308 --> 01:13:59,435
and kind of nonchalantly.

1594
01:14:00,018 --> 01:14:03,105
Do you get close with someone
you met for the first time?

1595
01:14:03,188 --> 01:14:05,357
<i>Because I'm not good at that.</i>

1596
01:14:05,441 --> 01:14:11,363
<i>When someone appears to be alone</i>
<i>or can't join the conversation,</i>

1597
01:14:11,447 --> 01:14:14,825
<i>I appreciated how you picked up on that</i>
<i>and tried to include them.</i>

1598
01:14:16,160 --> 01:14:18,787
I've never seen ChatGPT catch bugs.

1599
01:14:19,455 --> 01:14:22,875
-If you get the paid version, they do.
-They catch bugs for you?

1600
01:14:22,958 --> 01:14:24,501
When you told me your ideal type,

1601
01:14:24,585 --> 01:14:28,130
you said the person looks beautiful
when they shine.

1602
01:14:28,213 --> 01:14:31,633
There is a moment
when that person really shines,

1603
01:14:31,717 --> 01:14:33,343
and that's when they look so beautiful

1604
01:14:34,136 --> 01:14:35,804
even if they aren't that pretty.

1605
01:14:36,305 --> 01:14:37,848
It's something I would have said.

1606
01:14:38,682 --> 01:14:42,394
I was so surprised
when you said those words.

1607
01:14:43,604 --> 01:14:44,480
I liked it.

1608
01:14:46,023 --> 01:14:47,399
Honestly, I am

1609
01:14:48,275 --> 01:14:49,943
so jealous of people who can dance well.

1610
01:14:50,027 --> 01:14:51,361
So,

1611
01:14:51,445 --> 01:14:53,989
your looks plus your personality,

1612
01:14:54,072 --> 01:14:55,032
but on top of that,

1613
01:14:55,657 --> 01:14:57,826
you said that was your job.

1614
01:14:57,910 --> 01:14:59,870
That's why I totally

1615
01:14:59,953 --> 01:15:01,163
fell for you.

1616
01:15:01,246 --> 01:15:03,916
She should have said this from the start!

1617
01:15:03,999 --> 01:15:08,337
Why say that now?
The moment's already passed.

1618
01:15:08,420 --> 01:15:12,799
Do-geon kept telling her that
she should try to change his mind.

1619
01:15:12,883 --> 01:15:15,010
She must have gotten
the courage from that.

1620
01:15:16,220 --> 01:15:18,931
Do-geon messed everything up but…

1621
01:15:20,057 --> 01:15:21,475
-But this--
-Yeah, this one thing.

1622
01:15:21,558 --> 01:15:23,435
-He gave her the courage.
-He did.

1623
01:15:23,519 --> 01:15:24,728
That's huge.

1624
01:15:24,811 --> 01:15:26,813
That's why I totally

1625
01:15:26,897 --> 01:15:28,065
fell for you.

1626
01:15:30,359 --> 01:15:31,527
That's why

1627
01:15:31,610 --> 01:15:33,904
I'm going this far to explain myself.

1628
01:15:38,742 --> 01:15:41,912
<i>She made me feel at ease</i>
<i>while we had that conversation.</i>

1629
01:15:41,995 --> 01:15:44,790
I thought she was cool.

1630
01:15:44,873 --> 01:15:48,835
Even though I didn't intend it,
I did hurt her feelings.

1631
01:15:48,919 --> 01:15:51,922
Despite that,
the fact that she was able to say that…

1632
01:15:52,005 --> 01:15:54,383
I don't think I could've done that
if I were her.

1633
01:15:55,467 --> 01:15:56,843
From where I stand,

1634
01:15:59,096 --> 01:16:00,597
you are remarkable.

1635
01:16:00,681 --> 01:16:02,182
The way I want someone to be.

1636
01:16:03,350 --> 01:16:04,810
Then, let's be friends.

1637
01:16:04,893 --> 01:16:07,145
We can be friends. I tried today.

1638
01:16:07,229 --> 01:16:10,148
But I don't mean it
the way I said it last night.

1639
01:16:10,232 --> 01:16:11,817
The way you said it last night?

1640
01:16:11,900 --> 01:16:13,986
What do you mean now?

1641
01:16:14,069 --> 01:16:17,114
I want you to open up to me
just a little bit more.

1642
01:16:19,324 --> 01:16:21,243
Okay, I won't close the door on you.

1643
01:16:21,326 --> 01:16:22,869
I wanted to

1644
01:16:24,246 --> 01:16:26,957
try my best for a little longer.

1645
01:16:27,040 --> 01:16:29,418
But I'd like you to work with me a little.

1646
01:16:30,502 --> 01:16:31,378
Work with you…

1647
01:16:32,087 --> 01:16:33,005
I'll work with you.

1648
01:16:34,464 --> 01:16:37,259
I'll keep pushing myself to open up too.

1649
01:16:37,342 --> 01:16:41,305
<i>It felt like he respected</i>
<i>the weight of my feelings.</i>

1650
01:16:41,388 --> 01:16:44,224
As long as it's like this,
I can keep express how I feel to him.

1651
01:16:44,308 --> 01:16:48,854
I think it's a relationship
that's worth putting my feelings into.

1652
01:16:48,937 --> 01:16:52,024
I was able to express how I felt
as much as I wanted.

1653
01:16:52,691 --> 01:16:55,235
That made me feel better.

1654
01:16:55,819 --> 01:16:57,029
Ye-rim has matured.

1655
01:17:00,240 --> 01:17:02,409
THE SECRET DATE HAS ENDED

1656
01:17:03,368 --> 01:17:05,871
See you back at the house.

1657
01:17:06,622 --> 01:17:08,081
Anyway, I'll get going.

1658
01:17:13,378 --> 01:17:16,006
YE-RIM AND KYUNG-HO'S
SECRET DATE HAS ENDED

1659
01:17:16,548 --> 01:17:20,636
ALL THE SECRET DATES HAVE ENDED

1660
01:17:25,849 --> 01:17:28,644
KYUNG-HO IS BACK AT THE HOUSE FIRST

1661
01:17:54,503 --> 01:17:55,671
Do you know what time it is?

1662
01:17:56,838 --> 01:17:57,881
When did you get back?

1663
01:17:57,964 --> 01:17:59,383
I got back an hour ago.

1664
01:17:59,466 --> 01:18:00,967
-Really?
-No.

1665
01:18:01,051 --> 01:18:02,010
About ten minutes ago?

1666
01:18:02,094 --> 01:18:03,470
Why are you the only one back?

1667
01:18:03,553 --> 01:18:04,971
-I'm the only one here.
-Why?

1668
01:18:05,889 --> 01:18:07,891
-I don't know.
-Seriously?

1669
01:18:07,974 --> 01:18:09,267
Why would I lie?

1670
01:18:09,351 --> 01:18:10,727
-Really?
-Yeah.

1671
01:18:11,353 --> 01:18:12,729
Are you not happy about that?

1672
01:18:12,813 --> 01:18:14,272
-I'm happy.
-So happy, right?

1673
01:18:14,356 --> 01:18:15,399
I love it.

1674
01:18:16,233 --> 01:18:17,526
-Seriously?
-Yeah.

1675
01:18:17,609 --> 01:18:20,237
<i>We stayed at this house for five days,</i>

1676
01:18:20,320 --> 01:18:22,322
<i>so we got used to it.</i>

1677
01:18:24,741 --> 01:18:26,827
-I kicked everyone out.
-Good job.

1678
01:18:26,910 --> 01:18:28,036
I beat everyone.

1679
01:18:28,120 --> 01:18:29,037
-Really?
-Yeah.

1680
01:18:29,121 --> 01:18:31,289
<i>But most of the lights were off</i>

1681
01:18:31,373 --> 01:18:33,709
<i>and only the dim lights</i>

1682
01:18:33,792 --> 01:18:36,378
<i>were on in the hallway.</i>

1683
01:18:36,878 --> 01:18:39,297
<i>The atmosphere felt strangely different.</i>

1684
01:18:39,381 --> 01:18:41,049
Won't they be back in about ten minutes?

1685
01:18:42,092 --> 01:18:43,510
-What a shame.
-One by one.

1686
01:18:44,845 --> 01:18:46,471
<i>-Are you sad about that?</i>
<i>-Yeah.</i>

1687
01:18:46,555 --> 01:18:47,556
<i>Want something to drink?</i>

1688
01:18:49,474 --> 01:18:51,101
Were you able to organize your thoughts?

1689
01:18:51,184 --> 01:18:52,978
Yeah, a bit.

1690
01:18:54,646 --> 01:18:56,898
I really focused

1691
01:18:57,524 --> 01:18:59,443
on myself.

1692
01:19:01,278 --> 01:19:02,320
You see,

1693
01:19:03,363 --> 01:19:09,286
the way you express how you feel
is so different from how Jung-min does.

1694
01:19:10,620 --> 01:19:11,872
Which one do you prefer?

1695
01:19:11,955 --> 01:19:12,956
I know, right?

1696
01:19:17,711 --> 01:19:18,545
"I know, right?"

1697
01:19:24,718 --> 01:19:26,052
-Did you see it?
-Yeah.

1698
01:19:26,136 --> 01:19:29,347
It got upgraded. I was wondering
if there was something wrong with my eyes.

1699
01:19:29,431 --> 01:19:31,850
-There were colors.
-Yeah.

1700
01:19:31,933 --> 01:19:33,810
Then, I saw the heart.

1701
01:19:34,644 --> 01:19:36,354
Maybe you have better sense of style
than I do.

1702
01:19:36,438 --> 01:19:37,606
-Right?
-Yeah.

1703
01:19:37,689 --> 01:19:40,066
You knew how to use the red like this.

1704
01:19:43,737 --> 01:19:44,863
It's very…

1705
01:19:46,740 --> 01:19:48,992
-interesting.
-What is?

1706
01:19:49,075 --> 01:19:50,327
My feelings.

1707
01:19:53,246 --> 01:19:55,791
You aren't even going to tell me,
but you say it's interesting and fun.

1708
01:19:55,874 --> 01:19:59,544
Because I don't know yet.

1709
01:19:59,628 --> 01:20:00,962
-Okay.
-Yeah.

1710
01:20:05,967 --> 01:20:07,302
Do you know how to check someone's pulse?

1711
01:20:07,385 --> 01:20:08,720
No. How is it?

1712
01:20:08,804 --> 01:20:09,971
Isn't it beating fast?

1713
01:20:13,308 --> 01:20:15,519
-Isn't it beating really fast?
-It is. Why?

1714
01:20:17,979 --> 01:20:19,731
It's right here.

1715
01:20:20,273 --> 01:20:21,691
-Here?
-Yeah.

1716
01:20:21,775 --> 01:20:23,485
-Do you feel it when you press it?
-I do.

1717
01:20:24,444 --> 01:20:25,570
Yours is slow.

1718
01:20:25,654 --> 01:20:27,322
-It's slow?
-Yeah.

1719
01:20:28,573 --> 01:20:29,449
You're right.

1720
01:20:30,116 --> 01:20:31,117
Go.

1721
01:20:31,201 --> 01:20:32,369
-Yours is fast.
-Get out.

1722
01:20:32,452 --> 01:20:33,370
Yours is the fast one.

1723
01:20:36,081 --> 01:20:37,249
<i>I don't know.</i>

1724
01:20:38,500 --> 01:20:39,334
<i>It felt strange.</i>

1725
01:20:40,460 --> 01:20:41,795
<i>I felt dazed.</i>

1726
01:20:43,088 --> 01:20:45,382
<i>She may have captivated me</i>

1727
01:20:45,465 --> 01:20:49,094
<i>or I could have been captivated</i>
<i>by that place.</i>

1728
01:20:49,177 --> 01:20:52,472
<i>I felt like I didn't have</i>

1729
01:20:52,556 --> 01:20:55,976
<i>control over my own mind.</i>

1730
01:20:58,478 --> 01:20:59,646
-What about you?
-What?

1731
01:20:59,729 --> 01:21:01,565
You must have a lot on your mind.

1732
01:21:03,066 --> 01:21:04,943
Yeah, I had a lot on my mind.

1733
01:21:05,026 --> 01:21:07,028
But mine has been sorted out.

1734
01:21:09,114 --> 01:21:11,408
I don't know what I'm going to do,

1735
01:21:12,993 --> 01:21:15,245
but I know how I feel.

1736
01:21:19,749 --> 01:21:22,043
I'm just doing
what my heart tells me to do.

1737
01:21:23,128 --> 01:21:24,170
Good.

1738
01:21:24,254 --> 01:21:25,547
-Good?
-Yeah.

1739
01:21:25,630 --> 01:21:26,548
Me too.

1740
01:21:35,307 --> 01:21:37,350
This is fun, isn't it?

1741
01:21:38,602 --> 01:21:39,561
-Is it fun?
-Yeah.

1742
01:21:39,644 --> 01:21:40,478
How can it be fun?

1743
01:21:42,647 --> 01:21:45,108
-It isn't fun?
-It's fun.

1744
01:21:46,151 --> 01:21:47,903
I don't know anything, but it's fun.

1745
01:21:49,070 --> 01:21:50,363
You're the only one that knows.

1746
01:21:50,447 --> 01:21:52,782
-But it must be hard because you know.
-Yeah.

1747
01:21:55,911 --> 01:21:57,287
What should I do?

1748
01:21:58,246 --> 01:21:59,581
What is right?

1749
01:21:59,664 --> 01:22:01,708
Neither one is the right answer.

1750
01:22:01,791 --> 01:22:02,626
Then, what?

1751
01:22:02,709 --> 01:22:04,836
You're just picking

1752
01:22:07,380 --> 01:22:09,674
one from the two. Neither one is better.

1753
01:22:10,717 --> 01:22:13,929
Jung-min is clear
and straightforward in the way

1754
01:22:14,804 --> 01:22:15,680
he expresses himself.

1755
01:22:15,764 --> 01:22:17,390
Am I too indirect?

1756
01:22:18,099 --> 01:22:20,101
Well, you're similar.

1757
01:22:21,269 --> 01:22:23,688
-You are like this.
-Yeah.

1758
01:22:23,772 --> 01:22:25,231
Jung-min is like this.

1759
01:22:25,857 --> 01:22:26,858
-Really?
-Yeah.

1760
01:22:29,527 --> 01:22:30,445
I do go forward.

1761
01:22:32,113 --> 01:22:33,365
What if he's already there?

1762
01:22:33,448 --> 01:22:35,116
What if he came to me sooner?

1763
01:22:35,200 --> 01:22:37,327
Ah. Getting there fast doesn't matter.

1764
01:22:37,410 --> 01:22:38,954
You're the one who has to accept him.

1765
01:22:42,040 --> 01:22:44,584
-What if he won't give up?
-What?

1766
01:22:44,668 --> 01:22:46,044
What if he won't leave my side?

1767
01:22:46,127 --> 01:22:48,338
Then, I have to squeeze myself
between you two

1768
01:22:48,421 --> 01:22:50,131
if things get bad.

1769
01:22:50,215 --> 01:22:51,758
But he hasn't done that, has he?

1770
01:22:51,841 --> 01:22:53,301
What if he'll do that from now?

1771
01:22:53,385 --> 01:22:54,594
Then,

1772
01:22:54,678 --> 01:22:55,804
you come to me.

1773
01:22:56,513 --> 01:22:57,722
What if I don't want to do that?

1774
01:22:57,806 --> 01:22:59,307
-You don't?
-Yeah.

1775
01:22:59,391 --> 01:23:00,350
Can't you?

1776
01:23:02,310 --> 01:23:04,980
"I have to briefly go somewhere."

1777
01:23:05,063 --> 01:23:06,523
"Oh, right. I have to go change."

1778
01:23:06,606 --> 01:23:07,607
Then, come to me.

1779
01:23:09,859 --> 01:23:12,445
-Do we have to sit here and wait?
-Right?

1780
01:23:13,029 --> 01:23:15,031
I wish I could close the curtains here.

1781
01:23:15,115 --> 01:23:16,282
Close the curtains?

1782
01:23:16,366 --> 01:23:18,201
-Why?
-Do you want to kiss her?

1783
01:23:18,284 --> 01:23:20,120
Imagine there are curtains.

1784
01:23:26,668 --> 01:23:28,253
Let's run away to the tent.

1785
01:23:30,630 --> 01:23:33,049
-The tent that you hate so much.
-I know.

1786
01:23:33,133 --> 01:23:36,469
He should become king,
so the two of them can go to the tent.

1787
01:23:54,904 --> 01:23:57,782
YE-RIM IS BACK AT THE HOUSE

1788
01:23:57,866 --> 01:23:59,659
Your style is different today.

1789
01:23:59,743 --> 01:24:00,785
Today?

1790
01:24:00,869 --> 01:24:02,287
The boyfriend look.

1791
01:24:02,370 --> 01:24:04,080
Yeah, that was what I was going for.

1792
01:24:04,164 --> 01:24:05,457
A clean-cut look.

1793
01:24:11,671 --> 01:24:13,715
No, Ye-rim. No.

1794
01:24:13,798 --> 01:24:14,924
Go to the room!

1795
01:24:15,008 --> 01:24:16,176
Don't go to the living room!

1796
01:24:16,259 --> 01:24:18,511
-No, it's better to go to the living room!
-Don't go there!

1797
01:24:18,595 --> 01:24:19,429
Go to the room!

1798
01:24:19,512 --> 01:24:21,723
-It's better to go to the living room!
-Go to the room!

1799
01:24:21,806 --> 01:24:23,224
Did she see? Move away!

1800
01:24:27,437 --> 01:24:28,521
-Hey, Ye-rim.
-You're back.

1801
01:24:28,605 --> 01:24:29,439
Hi.

1802
01:24:37,947 --> 01:24:38,907
Why did you hit me?

1803
01:25:11,731 --> 01:25:12,857
Is she okay?

1804
01:25:12,941 --> 01:25:14,609
I want to give her a hug.

1805
01:25:17,445 --> 01:25:19,739
How did the situation end up like this?

1806
01:25:19,823 --> 01:25:22,617
My heart breaks for her. It aches.

1807
01:25:29,582 --> 01:25:31,960
-It looks good. Thank you.
-Thank you for the food.

1808
01:25:32,043 --> 01:25:33,753
So very, very much.

1809
01:25:35,130 --> 01:25:36,089
Why aren't you eating, Ga-yeon?

1810
01:25:36,673 --> 01:25:38,258
I'm full.

1811
01:25:40,343 --> 01:25:41,636
There's a tear on your shirt.

1812
01:25:42,470 --> 01:25:43,847
I'm going for the hot girl look.

1813
01:25:44,556 --> 01:25:46,015
-It's the hot girl look.
-Right.

1814
01:25:46,099 --> 01:25:47,767
-You look sexy.
-What's that?

1815
01:25:47,851 --> 01:25:48,935
Isn't it good?

1816
01:25:49,018 --> 01:25:49,894
Have some.

1817
01:25:49,978 --> 01:25:50,895
-Just a bit.
-I ate.

1818
01:25:50,979 --> 01:25:53,148
-Everyone lost weight.
-You already ate?

1819
01:25:53,231 --> 01:25:56,109
I ate a lot.

1820
01:26:01,614 --> 01:26:03,449
Did I look like this while playing <i>gonggi</i>?

1821
01:26:04,117 --> 01:26:05,034
When is that?

1822
01:26:07,787 --> 01:26:09,539
Why do I look so stupid?

1823
01:26:09,622 --> 01:26:10,582
Watch carefully.

1824
01:26:10,665 --> 01:26:14,085
THE PROBLEMATIC VIDEO
OF DO-GEON PLAYING GONGGI

1825
01:26:14,169 --> 01:26:16,588
You should've stopped me
before I did this.

1826
01:26:16,671 --> 01:26:19,549
-You should've stopped me.
-I'd make you do it more.

1827
01:26:19,632 --> 01:26:20,592
Do-geon playing…

1828
01:26:20,675 --> 01:26:22,635
-Do-geon playing <i>gonggi.</i>
<i>-</i>Do-geon playing <i>gonggi.</i>

1829
01:26:25,889 --> 01:26:27,473
Are you okay, sir?

1830
01:26:27,557 --> 01:26:29,142
Call an ambulance.

1831
01:26:29,225 --> 01:26:31,603
It's okay. It wasn't that bad.
It had a positive effect.

1832
01:26:32,312 --> 01:26:34,147
If anything, it makes you more human.

1833
01:26:34,230 --> 01:26:35,982
If I got one…

1834
01:26:36,065 --> 01:26:38,276
Have a drink at the lounge?

1835
01:26:38,359 --> 01:26:39,861
Drink at the lounge?

1836
01:26:40,445 --> 01:26:42,238
Why is he so funny?

1837
01:26:42,322 --> 01:26:43,364
Drink whenever we meet?

1838
01:26:50,121 --> 01:26:52,165
Is this your first meal
since this morning?

1839
01:26:52,832 --> 01:26:54,292
Isn't that right?

1840
01:26:54,375 --> 01:26:55,627
You didn't eat?

1841
01:26:55,710 --> 01:26:58,463
<i>I regretted and was disappointed in myself</i>

1842
01:26:58,546 --> 01:27:00,840
<i>that I wasn't more specific.</i>

1843
01:27:00,924 --> 01:27:05,053
<i>I could have been more specific</i>
<i>about how it has been</i>

1844
01:27:05,762 --> 01:27:07,096
<i>tough for me.</i>

1845
01:27:09,557 --> 01:27:11,476
What do you like most? Come on. Stop.

1846
01:27:12,769 --> 01:27:14,187
-Are you okay?
-Yeah.

1847
01:27:14,896 --> 01:27:15,855
What's up?

1848
01:27:16,439 --> 01:27:17,357
I have indigestion.

1849
01:27:17,440 --> 01:27:18,691
It's here.

1850
01:27:18,775 --> 01:27:20,109
I took medicine twice.

1851
01:27:20,193 --> 01:27:21,736
I took it on an empty stomach.

1852
01:27:21,819 --> 01:27:23,780
I feel much better now.

1853
01:27:23,863 --> 01:27:25,198
-You okay?
-Glad to hear that.

1854
01:27:26,491 --> 01:27:28,368
HE HAS A LETTER IN HIS HAND

1855
01:27:28,451 --> 01:27:29,744
What could it be?

1856
01:27:29,827 --> 01:27:32,080
Du-dum.

1857
01:27:32,163 --> 01:27:33,081
What could it be?

1858
01:27:33,164 --> 01:27:34,499
-Read it, Jung-min.
-What is it?

1859
01:27:34,582 --> 01:27:36,417
-What? What is it now?
-What is it?

1860
01:27:36,501 --> 01:27:38,878
"The game will begin.
Go to the lounge now."

1861
01:27:38,962 --> 01:27:40,255
-Really?
-Love Marble.

1862
01:27:40,338 --> 01:27:41,172
Love Marble?

1863
01:27:41,256 --> 01:27:42,590
What is that?

1864
01:27:42,674 --> 01:27:44,509
Not Blue Marble, but Love Marble?

1865
01:27:47,178 --> 01:27:48,012
Joo-heon!

1866
01:27:48,096 --> 01:27:50,515
This game had so much physical contact.
They were holding hands and everything.

1867
01:27:50,598 --> 01:27:52,183
-Yeah.
-Remember the coffee-coated peanut?

1868
01:27:52,267 --> 01:27:54,143
The worlds are all connected.
It's behind us.

1869
01:27:54,727 --> 01:27:55,687
This one.

1870
01:27:56,354 --> 01:27:58,564
-Let's watch. This should be fun.
-This is insane.

1871
01:27:58,648 --> 01:28:01,192
They're going all out on their last night.

1872
01:28:03,236 --> 01:28:06,030
<i>On this final night,</i>
<i>we will now play Love Marble.</i>

1873
01:28:06,864 --> 01:28:08,616
<i>-What do you think about me?</i>
<i>-You're pretty.</i>

1874
01:28:08,700 --> 01:28:09,659
<i>I was dumbfounded.</i>

1875
01:28:09,742 --> 01:28:11,828
Who takes first place in your heart?

1876
01:28:11,911 --> 01:28:12,870
Well…

1877
01:28:12,954 --> 01:28:15,873
<i>I was confident that she'd choose me.</i>

1878
01:28:15,957 --> 01:28:17,583
<i>Is it over for me?</i>

1879
01:28:17,667 --> 01:28:20,003
<i>That was when I was</i>
<i>most overwhelmed with excitement.</i>

1880
01:28:20,086 --> 01:28:21,963
<i>Should I give him Heart Chip votes?</i>

1881
01:28:22,046 --> 01:28:24,757
There are some who are
contemplating leaving some or not.

1882
01:28:24,841 --> 01:28:25,967
He held my hand.

1883
01:28:26,050 --> 01:28:29,887
My heart raced more
when Jung-min held my hand.

1884
01:28:29,971 --> 01:28:30,847
I want to come in.

1885
01:28:30,930 --> 01:28:33,558
<i>I wanted the two of us to have a chat.</i>

1886
01:28:33,641 --> 01:28:34,600
This is really irritating.

1887
01:28:34,684 --> 01:28:36,227
Geez, this is so frustrating.

1888
01:28:36,311 --> 01:28:37,520
-To the tent?
-For real?

1889
01:28:37,603 --> 01:28:39,105
They already closed the tent.

1890
01:28:39,188 --> 01:28:40,898
<i>-You're right.</i>
<i>-That's insane.</i>

1891
01:28:40,982 --> 01:28:42,066
I can't control myself.

1892
01:28:43,192 --> 01:28:44,652
<i>"It's the day of the final decision."</i>

1893
01:28:44,736 --> 01:28:46,487
<i>"Confess how you feel."</i>

1894
01:28:46,571 --> 01:28:49,741
<i>Did the subjects,</i>
<i>who always get what they want, win…</i>

1895
01:28:49,824 --> 01:28:52,368
<i>I wanted to be true to my feelings</i>
<i>until the end.</i>

1896
01:28:52,952 --> 01:28:55,204
<i>…the love they were after?</i>

1897
01:28:55,288 --> 01:28:57,957
<i>When you gain something,</i>
<i>you lose something too.</i>

1898
01:28:58,958 --> 01:29:01,085
<i>The final decision will begin.</i>

1899
01:29:11,220 --> 01:29:13,222
Subtitle translation by: Ilyoung Kim

1900
01:29:13,306 --> 01:29:16,142
THE LOVE LAB
